ace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/0.98 relative rounded-[22px] px-4 py-2.5 leading-6 max-w-(--user-chat-width,70%)"><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">I've already connected github with chatgpt, and you have access...</div></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex justify-end"><div aria-label="Your message actions" class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto touch:opacity-100 duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" role="group" tabindex="-1" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy message" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Edit message" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#6d87e1" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div><span class="sr-only"><br></span></section><section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="bf60a597-3c26-459a-a752-d2fdfeb156b8" data-testid="conversation-turn-6" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h4 class="sr-only select-none">ChatGPT said:</h4><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><span class="group/tool-message"><span class="block first:mt-0 relative text-token-text-secondary hover:text-token-text-primary my-1.5"><div class="group start-0 top-0 me-1.5 overflow-hidden mt-1 text-start"><button class="inline-block" style="opacity: 1;"><div class="flex items-center justify-start gap-1"><span class="text-start">Called tool</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ba3792" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></div></button></div></span></span><div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap gap-2 empty:hidden"></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><button type="button" class="text-token-text-tertiary flex items-center gap-0.5 dark:text-(--interactive-label-tertiary-default) hover:text-token-text-primary dark:hover:text-token-text-primary">Thought for 9m 53s<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon-xs"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#b140e7" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="bd22b030-4009-4b92-bb00-b929aaa1683a" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-4-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="376">I can see the repo connection, and I verified the repository exists as <code data-start="71" data-end="97">dylanlmeraki/last_breath</code> on <code data-start="101" data-end="107">main</code>. What I could <strong data-start="122" data-end="129">not</strong> get from this session was the actual file tree / code contents through the GitHub connector, so I cannot honestly claim a repo-level audit yet. The connector is resolving the repo, but the content-browsing/code-search side is not returning files.</p>
<p data-start="378" data-end="389">That means:</p>
<ul data-start="391" data-end="615">
<li data-section-id="1btoaac" data-start="391" data-end="496">
<p data-start="393" data-end="496">I can give you a solid <strong data-start="416" data-end="466">site/brand/IA/homepage strategy assessment now</strong> from the assets you attached.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1hcusma" data-start="497" data-end="615">
<p data-start="499" data-end="615">I cannot yet do the <strong data-start="519" data-end="579">surgical monorepo trim plan against actual folders/files</strong> until I can read the repo contents.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="y0q8vw" data-start="617" data-end="647">What the branding is saying</h2>
<p data-start="649" data-end="762">Across the live-site screenshot, the redesign captures, and the uploaded one-pager, the brand is very consistent:</p>
<ul data-start="764" data-end="1027">
<li data-section-id="25wvz0" data-start="764" data-end="810">
<p data-start="766" data-end="810"><strong data-start="766" data-end="789">Primary foundation:</strong> deep navy / ink blue</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1mbydgv" data-start="811" data-end="859">
<p data-start="813" data-end="859"><strong data-start="813" data-end="832">Primary accent:</strong> bright construction orange</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="m0vyup" data-start="860" data-end="904">
<p data-start="862" data-end="904"><strong data-start="862" data-end="883">Secondary accent:</strong> electric blue / cyan</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ee9u7m" data-start="905" data-end="944">
<p data-start="907" data-end="944"><strong data-start="907" data-end="933">Support/status accent:</strong> teal-green</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1lh93n2" data-start="945" data-end="991">
<p data-start="947" data-end="991"><strong data-start="947" data-end="963">Base canvas:</strong> very light gray / off-white</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="10gdgrr" data-start="992" data-end="1027">
<p data-start="994" data-end="1027"><strong data-start="994" data-end="1003">Text:</strong> dark slate / blue-black</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1029" data-end="1089">From the visuals, the palette reads approximately like this:</p>
<div class="TyagGW_tableContainer"><div tabindex="-1" class="group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit"><table data-start="1091" data-end="1424" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="1091" data-end="1114"><tr data-start="1091" data-end="1114"><th data-start="1091" data-end="1098" data-col-size="sm" class="">Role</th><th data-start="1098" data-end="1114" data-col-size="sm" class="">Approx color</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="1125" data-end="1424"><tr data-start="1125" data-end="1169"><td data-start="1125" data-end="1143" data-col-size="sm">Deep brand navy</td><td data-start="1143" data-end="1169" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="1145" data-end="1154">#121D34</code> to <code data-start="1158" data-end="1167">#182238</code></td></tr><tr data-start="1170" data-end="1218"><td data-start="1170" data-end="1192" data-col-size="sm">Secondary dark navy</td><td data-start="1192" data-end="1218" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="1194" data-end="1203">#1D2435</code> to <code data-start="1207" data-end="1216">#22314A</code></td></tr><tr data-start="1219" data-end="1258"><td data-start="1219" data-end="1232" data-col-size="sm">CTA orange</td><td data-start="1232" data-end="1258" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="1234" data-end="1243">#E97323</code> to <code data-start="1247" data-end="1256">#F58220</code></td></tr><tr data-start="1259" data-end="1306"><td data-start="1259" data-end="1280" data-col-size="sm">Bright cyan / blue</td><td data-start="1280" data-end="1306" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="1282" data-end="1291">#1EA2D3</code> to <code data-start="1295" data-end="1304">#3295FF</code></td></tr><tr data-start="1307" data-end="1359"><td data-start="1307" data-end="1333" data-col-size="sm">Teal / completion state</td><td data-start="1333" data-end="1359" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="1335" data-end="1344">#31C5B4</code> to <code data-start="1348" data-end="1357">#33C6B2</code></td></tr><tr data-start="1360" data-end="1392"><td data-start="1360" data-end="1379" data-col-size="sm">Light background</td><td data-start="1379" data-end="1392" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="1381" data-end="1390">#F6F8FA</code></td></tr><tr data-start="1393" data-end="1424"><td data-start="1393" data-end="1411" data-col-size="sm">Body copy slate</td><td data-start="1411" data-end="1424" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="1413" data-end="1422">#66738A</code></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<p data-start="1426" data-end="1885">The uploaded PDF reinforces the positioning very clearly: the firm is framed as <strong data-start="1506" data-end="1546">“Consulting Engineers &amp; Contractors”</strong>, with four main service pillars — <strong data-start="1581" data-end="1677">Construction Service, Engineering Consulting, Inspections &amp; Testing, and Stormwater Planning</strong> — and the differentiators are <strong data-start="1708" data-end="1847">field reality, Bay Area jurisdictional familiarity, compliance-minded delivery, in-house PE/QSD/QSP capability, and Class A/B licensing</strong> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_2ir_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span></p>
<p data-start="1887" data-end="1981">That is the core trust language. It is much stronger than generic construction-marketing copy.</p>
<hr data-start="1983" data-end="1986">
<h2 data-section-id="1gw78m7" data-start="1988" data-end="2006">My main finding</h2>
<p data-start="2008" data-end="2071">Your instincts are correct: this should <strong data-start="2048" data-end="2055">not</strong> be an overhaul.</p>
<p data-start="2073" data-end="2133">The redesign assets are strongest when they do three things:</p>
<ol data-start="2135" data-end="2265">
<li data-section-id="1wdzhkw" data-start="2135" data-end="2171">
<p data-start="2138" data-end="2171"><strong data-start="2138" data-end="2171">Compress trust signals upward</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="cyh05i" data-start="2172" data-end="2213">
<p data-start="2175" data-end="2213"><strong data-start="2175" data-end="2213">Make project evidence more visible</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="11pnwqw" data-start="2214" data-end="2265">
<p data-start="2217" data-end="2265"><strong data-start="2217" data-end="2265">Keep the visual system calm and professional</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2267" data-end="2444">For your audience — GCs, supers, architects, engineers, construction professionals — trust is built less by broad brand storytelling and more by fast answers to these questions:</p>
<ul data-start="2446" data-end="2726">
<li data-section-id="qu4lkw" data-start="2446" data-end="2498">
<p data-start="2448" data-end="2498">Can these people actually execute in the Bay Area?</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="8k4t9l" data-start="2499" data-end="2574">
<p data-start="2501" data-end="2574">Do they understand permitting, phasing, field conditions, and compliance?</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ym4y4j" data-start="2575" data-end="2632">
<p data-start="2577" data-end="2632">Can they support active jobs without creating friction?</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="8ytakx" data-start="2633" data-end="2691">
<p data-start="2635" data-end="2691">Do they have project evidence near my geography / scope?</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="18jycbe" data-start="2692" data-end="2726">
<p data-start="2694" data-end="2726">Can I get a real person quickly?</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2728" data-end="2871">That means the highest-value homepage additions are <strong data-start="2780" data-end="2787">not</strong> the full testimonial slider or the full estimator. The highest-value additions are:</p>
<ul data-start="2873" data-end="3048">
<li data-section-id="43g6fv" data-start="2873" data-end="2911">
<p data-start="2875" data-end="2911">a <strong data-start="2877" data-end="2911">proof rail directly under hero</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1n18hud" data-start="2912" data-end="2982">
<p data-start="2914" data-end="2982">a <strong data-start="2916" data-end="2982">condensed project evidence module with map + rotating snippets</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1og6a6c" data-start="2983" data-end="3017">
<p data-start="2985" data-end="3017">a <strong data-start="2987" data-end="3017">tight relevant-work teaser</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15ysopp" data-start="3018" data-end="3048">
<p data-start="3020" data-end="3048">a <strong data-start="3022" data-end="3048">delivery/process strip</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3050" data-end="3053">
<h2 data-section-id="vhur2x" data-start="3055" data-end="3088">Recommended homepage structure</h2>
<h3 data-section-id="1kkbirt" data-start="3090" data-end="3101">1. Hero</h3>
<p data-start="3102" data-end="3199">Keep the existing hero pattern. It already has the right job: credibility, scale, and direct CTA.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="54v9zh" data-start="3201" data-end="3251">2. Add a proof rail immediately under the hero</h3>
<p data-start="3252" data-end="3275">This is your best move.</p>
<p data-start="3277" data-end="3338">Do it as a <strong data-start="3288" data-end="3320">single horizontal proof line</strong>, not large cards.</p>
<p data-start="3340" data-end="3391">Use 5–6 compact items, separated visually, such as:</p>
<ul data-start="3393" data-end="3603">
<li data-section-id="mpplfs" data-start="3393" data-end="3424">
<p data-start="3395" data-end="3424">40+ years Bay Area experience</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="14wv3ac" data-start="3425" data-end="3465">
<p data-start="3427" data-end="3465">In-house engineering + field execution</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ftzzsl" data-start="3466" data-end="3488">
<p data-start="3468" data-end="3488">Class A / B licensed</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1fjdzt2" data-start="3489" data-end="3513">
<p data-start="3491" data-end="3513">PE / QSD / QSP support</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="gsryog" data-start="3514" data-end="3550">
<p data-start="3516" data-end="3550">Public works + commercial delivery</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="119xwiy" data-start="3551" data-end="3603">
<p data-start="3553" data-end="3603">Inspection, compliance, and closeout documentation</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3605" data-end="3694">This works because it answers competence questions before the user scrolls into the body.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="184hqdy" data-start="3696" data-end="3720">3. Core capabilities</h3>
<p data-start="3721" data-end="3825">Keep the capability cards, but tighten the copy so each reads more operationally and less descriptively.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="7vy7of" data-start="3827" data-end="3867">4. Condensed project evidence module</h3>
<p data-start="3868" data-end="3921">This should come much earlier than a typical gallery.</p>
<p data-start="3923" data-end="3942"><strong data-start="3923" data-end="3942">Desktop layout:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3943" data-end="4016">
<li data-section-id="1y9q52j" data-start="3943" data-end="3981">
<p data-start="3945" data-end="3981">Left: rotating project snippet stack</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="nlfs0p" data-start="3982" data-end="4016">
<p data-start="3984" data-end="4016">Right: condensed interactive map</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4018" data-end="4055">Each rotating snippet should include:</p>
<ul data-start="4056" data-end="4136">
<li data-section-id="128ddju" data-start="4056" data-end="4070">
<p data-start="4058" data-end="4070">project name</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="whxzxx" data-start="4071" data-end="4081">
<p data-start="4073" data-end="4081">location</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="lz7h6t" data-start="4082" data-end="4100">
<p data-start="4084" data-end="4100">service category</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1lpej18" data-start="4101" data-end="4109">
<p data-start="4103" data-end="4109">status</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="13f7mr2" data-start="4110" data-end="4136">
<p data-start="4112" data-end="4136">one-line proof statement</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4138" data-end="4156">Example structure:</p>
<ul data-start="4157" data-end="4305">
<li data-section-id="bwjml2" data-start="4157" data-end="4197">
<p data-start="4159" data-end="4197"><em data-start="4159" data-end="4197">Seismic Retrofit - Parking Structure</em></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="19ao06h" data-start="4198" data-end="4214">
<p data-start="4200" data-end="4214"><em data-start="4200" data-end="4214">San Jose, CA</em></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="uf6na8" data-start="4215" data-end="4255">
<p data-start="4217" data-end="4255"><em data-start="4217" data-end="4255">Infrastructure / Active-site phasing</em></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="lyhxh6" data-start="4256" data-end="4305">
<p data-start="4258" data-end="4305"><em data-start="4258" data-end="4305">Kept structure partially open during delivery</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4307" data-end="4405">The map should be visibly tied to the snippet state. When the snippet rotates, the marker updates.</p>
<p data-start="4407" data-end="4515">Do <strong data-start="4410" data-end="4417">not</strong> put the full county list or full filter system on home. Save that for Projects / About / Contact.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="nzf5dv" data-start="4517" data-end="4549">5. Relevant work grid teaser</h3>
<p data-start="4550" data-end="4622">A smaller version of the gallery is good on home, but keep it selective:</p>
<ul data-start="4623" data-end="4706">
<li data-section-id="12mmrbx" data-start="4623" data-end="4645">
<p data-start="4625" data-end="4645">6 featured cards max</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="yl4t85" data-start="4646" data-end="4676">
<p data-start="4648" data-end="4676">strong service/location tags</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1sfqq4r" data-start="4677" data-end="4706">
<p data-start="4679" data-end="4706">CTA to full project gallery</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="2r2vuh" data-start="4708" data-end="4729">6. How we deliver</h3>
<p data-start="4730" data-end="4864">The dark-band process strip from the redesign is useful. It translates well for professional buyers because it signals predictability.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="w5nos8" data-start="4866" data-end="4889">7. Team credibility</h3>
<p data-start="4890" data-end="4972">Use a <strong data-start="4896" data-end="4918">small expert strip</strong>, not the full people grid on home.<br>
Show 3 people max.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="web3rb" data-start="4974" data-end="4992">8. Testimonial</h3>
<p data-start="4993" data-end="5112">Use one short testimonial block, low on the page.<br>
For this audience, testimonials should support proof, not lead proof.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="184qt49" data-start="5114" data-end="5134">9. CTA / inquiry</h3>
<p data-start="5135" data-end="5176">The large contact block is good. Keep it.</p>
<hr data-start="5178" data-end="5181">
<h2 data-section-id="ijmgl1" data-start="5183" data-end="5237"><span role="text">What I would <em data-start="5199" data-end="5204">not</em> prioritize on the homepage first</span></h2>
<h3 data-section-id="2gsdiz" data-start="5239" data-end="5257">Full estimator</h3>
<p data-start="5258" data-end="5372">Useful, but second phase.<br>
It is better as a dedicated page teaser than as a major home-page interaction right now.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="ies4sy" data-start="5374" data-end="5403">Full testimonial carousel</h3>
<p data-start="5404" data-end="5446">Too much weight for too little trust gain.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="nb72xs" data-start="5448" data-end="5471">Full project map UI</h3>
<p data-start="5472" data-end="5528">Too heavy for home. Keep the homepage version condensed.</p>
<hr data-start="5530" data-end="5533">
<h2 data-section-id="2r4f8c" data-start="5535" data-end="5556">Component guidance</h2>
<h2 data-section-id="1k9mnm5" data-start="5558" data-end="5572">Proof strip</h2>
<p data-start="5573" data-end="5623">Design it as a <strong data-start="5588" data-end="5602">trust rail</strong>, not a feature list.</p>
<p data-start="5625" data-end="5629">Use:</p>
<ul data-start="5630" data-end="5745">
<li data-section-id="1kteyd3" data-start="5630" data-end="5645">
<p data-start="5632" data-end="5645">compact icons</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="dapbl6" data-start="5646" data-end="5676">
<p data-start="5648" data-end="5676">bold label + short qualifier</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="m6mjb1" data-start="5677" data-end="5711">
<p data-start="5679" data-end="5711">one-row desktop / two-row mobile</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="rtbl09" data-start="5712" data-end="5725">
<p data-start="5714" data-end="5725">no carousel</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="y9co6p" data-start="5726" data-end="5745">
<p data-start="5728" data-end="5745">no long sentences</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="ivsqz7" data-start="5747" data-end="5771">Condensed project map</h2>
<p data-start="5772" data-end="5830">This is likely your highest-value new home-page component.</p>
<p data-start="5832" data-end="5848">Use these rules:</p>
<ul data-start="5849" data-end="6046">
<li data-section-id="1cbfnrx" data-start="5849" data-end="5880">
<p data-start="5851" data-end="5880">4–6 visible rotating snippets</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="8r6cdf" data-start="5881" data-end="5904">
<p data-start="5883" data-end="5904">sync snippet + marker</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="o2397" data-start="5905" data-end="5948">
<p data-start="5907" data-end="5948">keep filters minimal or omit them on home</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1j2jjs7" data-start="5949" data-end="6046">
<p data-start="5951" data-end="5986">use the status colors consistently:</p>
<ul data-start="5989" data-end="6046">
<li data-section-id="1m1snqf" data-start="5989" data-end="6004">
<p data-start="5991" data-end="6004">active = blue</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="18oqobo" data-start="6007" data-end="6025">
<p data-start="6009" data-end="6025">completed = teal</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="g4rzu4" data-start="6028" data-end="6046">
<p data-start="6030" data-end="6046">ongoing = orange</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="jcvwvl" data-start="6048" data-end="6072">“Relevant work” cards</h2>
<p data-start="6073" data-end="6149">The redesign cards are good because they feel like evidence, not decoration.</p>
<p data-start="6151" data-end="6156">Keep:</p>
<ul data-start="6157" data-end="6213">
<li data-section-id="1i4pyyi" data-start="6157" data-end="6172">
<p data-start="6159" data-end="6172">project image</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15j8uw7" data-start="6173" data-end="6186">
<p data-start="6175" data-end="6186">service tag</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1hvdobh" data-start="6187" data-end="6202">
<p data-start="6189" data-end="6202">project title</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="whxzxx" data-start="6203" data-end="6213">
<p data-start="6205" data-end="6213">location</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6215" data-end="6266">Avoid adding too much metadata on the home version.</p>
<hr data-start="6268" data-end="6271">
<h2 data-section-id="1wz9lca" data-start="6273" data-end="6295">Repo trim direction</h2>
<p data-start="6297" data-end="6386">Until I can inspect the codebase, this is the structure I would push toward conceptually:</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="6388" data-end="6659"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy"><div class="cm-scroller"><div class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly"><span>apps/</span><br><span>  marketing-site/</span><br><span>  internal-portal/</span><br><span>  client-portal/</span><br><br><span>services/</span><br><span>  marketing-api/</span><br><span>  internal-api/</span><br><span>  client-api/</span><br><br><span>packages/</span><br><span>  ui-marketing/</span><br><span>  ui-portal/</span><br><span>  brand-tokens/</span><br><span>  maps/</span><br><span>  forms/</span><br><span>  auth/</span><br><span>  data/</span><br><br><span>docs/</span><br><span>  marketing/</span><br><span>  internal/</span><br><span>  client/</span><br><span>  archive/</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="6661" data-end="6727">What should probably be removed or archived once I can inspect it:</p>
<ul data-start="6729" data-end="6963">
<li data-section-id="10eb0jy" data-start="6729" data-end="6751">
<p data-start="6731" data-end="6751">old experiment pages</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1kephjw" data-start="6752" data-end="6770">
<p data-start="6754" data-end="6770">duplicate assets</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="19pg03t" data-start="6771" data-end="6818">
<p data-start="6773" data-end="6818">screenshots/mockups living in runtime folders</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1imsr58" data-start="6819" data-end="6841">
<p data-start="6821" data-end="6841">dead shared packages</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="kjv9ze" data-start="6842" data-end="6874">
<p data-start="6844" data-end="6874">duplicated auth/data utilities</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="g5lznh" data-start="6875" data-end="6897">
<p data-start="6877" data-end="6897">abandoned prototypes</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1iiqg77" data-start="6898" data-end="6914">
<p data-start="6900" data-end="6914">backup folders</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="5czqgh" data-start="6915" data-end="6963">
<p data-start="6917" data-end="6963">one-off docs mixed into deployable app folders</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6965" data-end="7007">The goal is simple: keep only what serves:</p>
<ul data-start="7009" data-end="7104">
<li data-section-id="1ms5ax3" data-start="7009" data-end="7025">
<p data-start="7011" data-end="7025">marketing site</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="7if9az" data-start="7026" data-end="7043">
<p data-start="7028" data-end="7043">internal portal</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="9cxzlx" data-start="7044" data-end="7059">
<p data-start="7046" data-end="7059">client portal</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1xxd9wd" data-start="7060" data-end="7076">
<p data-start="7062" data-end="7076">their backends</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="wzcg86" data-start="7077" data-end="7104">
<p data-start="7079" data-end="7104">genuinely shared packages</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="7106" data-end="7158">Everything else should become archive or be deleted.</p>
<hr data-start="7160" data-end="7163">
<h2 data-section-id="1msgxz8" data-start="7165" data-end="7179">Bottom line</h2>
<p data-start="7181" data-end="7303">Your redesign direction is good. The strongest improvement is <strong data-start="7243" data-end="7250">not</strong> “more design.” It is <strong data-start="7272" data-end="7302">better sequencing of proof</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="7305" data-end="7335">The homepage should move from:</p>
<p data-start="7337" data-end="7371"><strong data-start="7337" data-end="7371">brand → services → more detail</strong></p>
<p data-start="7373" data-end="7376">to:</p>
<p data-start="7378" data-end="7449"><strong data-start="7378" data-end="7449">brand → proof → project evidence → services → delivery method → CTA</strong></p>
<p data-start="7451" data-end="7491">That is the right order for your buyers.</p>
<p data-start="7493" data-end="7749" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">For the repo itself, I still need actual content access to do a real trim/read-through. The fastest way to unblock that is to upload the repo zip here or re-select the repo directly into this chat’s GitHub context so I can read the tree and map exact cuts.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="relative h-[60px] select-none"><div class="absolute h-[60px]" style="opacity: 1;"><button class="not-prose group/footnote border-token-border-default bg-token-main-surface-primary hover:bg-token-main-surface-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 mt-3 mb-2 flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl border py-2 ps-3 pe-2.5"><div class="text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-0.5 text-xs font-semibold">Sources</div></button></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div aria-label="Response actions" class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" role="group" tabindex="-1" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy response" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"