tes-core-a066ed1a.svg#b140e7" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="b0384f5c-90ea-4bca-8324-42f8036f67c3" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-4-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="101">The GitHub app is connected, but this chat still does <strong data-start="54" data-end="61">not</strong> have the repo selected for code search.</p>
<p data-start="103" data-end="214">I tried the repo search and got a <code data-start="137" data-end="165">MissingGithubRepoSelection</code> error. To let me do the deep dive, in this chat:</p>
<ol data-start="216" data-end="299">
<li data-section-id="dfv5rb" data-start="216" data-end="233">
<p data-start="219" data-end="233">Type <code data-start="224" data-end="233">@github</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1iiz9b4" data-start="234" data-end="262">
<p data-start="237" data-end="262">Click the <strong data-start="247" data-end="257">GitHub</strong> icon</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1y657op" data-start="263" data-end="299">
<p data-start="266" data-end="299">Select <code data-start="273" data-end="299">dylanlmeraki/last_breath</code></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="301" data-end="366">Or use the <strong data-start="312" data-end="317">+</strong> button, choose <strong data-start="333" data-end="343">GitHub</strong>, and select that repo.</p>
<p data-start="368" data-end="424">Once that repo is selected here, I can do the full pass:</p>
<ul data-start="425" data-end="673">
<li data-section-id="1hye1ug" data-start="425" data-end="447">
<p data-start="427" data-end="447">repo structure audit</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1f2gk6c" data-start="448" data-end="518">
