ive flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><span class="group/tool-message"><span class="block first:mt-0 relative text-token-text-secondary hover:text-token-text-primary my-1.5"><div class="group start-0 top-0 me-1.5 overflow-hidden mt-1 text-start"><button class="inline-block" style="opacity: 1;"><div class="flex items-center justify-start gap-1"><span class="text-start">Called tool</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ba3792" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></div></button></div></span></span><div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap gap-2 empty:hidden"></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><button type="button" class="text-token-text-tertiary flex items-center gap-0.5 dark:text-(--interactive-label-tertiary-default) hover:text-token-text-primary dark:hover:text-token-text-primary">Thought for 59s<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon-xs"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#b140e7" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="6588aee2-a099-4ed2-9c33-67cca110989e" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-4-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="96">I checked again. The blocker is <strong data-start="32" data-end="55">not GitHub indexing</strong>. It is this chat’s repo-selection state.</p>
<p data-start="98" data-end="332">The code search connector is still returning <strong data-start="143" data-end="175"><code data-start="145" data-end="173">MissingGithubRepoSelection</code></strong>, which means the repo has not been granted to this conversation’s GitHub search context yet. That is separate from the repo being connected to your account.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="10sdyk9" data-start="334" data-end="356">What I did get done</h2>
<p data-start="358" data-end="703">I used the attached <code data-start="378" data-end="393">skill (1).zip</code> and read the bundled <code data-start="415" data-end="444">github-repo-reader/SKILL.md</code>. It is a good operating pattern: acquire a local snapshot of the repo, build an index, run local snippet search, then build context packs for deeper reasoning. I can use that workflow as soon as I can actually fetch the repository contents into this session.</p>
<p data-start="705" data-end="933">I also verified your <strong data-start="726" data-end="735">Figma</strong> access is available from here, and I can work against your team space. So once we have a file, node, or community reference, I can use Figma directly for component development and brand adaptation.</p>
<hr data-start="935" data-end="938">
<h1 data-section-id="hun066" data-start="940" data-end="960">Deep dive, phase 1</h1>
<p data-start="961" data-end="1020">This is the strongest assessment I can give right now from:</p>
<ul data-start="1022" data-end="1124">
<li data-section-id="1b0ogc" data-start="1022" data-end="1049">
<p data-start="1024" data-end="1049">your attached screenshots</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="9hos05" data-start="1050" data-end="1073">
<p data-start="1052" data-end="1073">the live-site capture</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="c0xyli" data-start="1074" data-end="1104">
<p data-start="1076" data-end="1104">the uploaded one-pager / PDF</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="mxjwak" data-start="1105" data-end="1124">
<p data-start="1107" data-end="1124">your stated goals</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1126" data-end="1570">The PDF establishes the core positioning clearly: <strong data-start="1176" data-end="1214">Consulting Engineers &amp; Contractors</strong>, with four pillars — <strong data-start="1236" data-end="1328">Construction Service, Engineering Consulting, Inspections &amp; Testing, Stormwater Planning</strong> — plus differentiators around <strong data-start="1359" data-end="1445">field-reality, Bay Area jurisdictional familiarity, and compliance-minded delivery</strong>. Those are your strongest trust levers and should be surfaced earlier on the homepage. <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_2js_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span></p>
<hr data-start="1572" data-end="1575">
<h2 data-section-id="2uxsyx" data-start="1577" data-end="1620">1. Brand system: what is already working</h2>
<p data-start="1622" data-end="1751">Your visual system is already coherent. It does <strong data-start="1670" data-end="1677">not</strong> need rebranding. It needs better hierarchy and better placement of proof.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="bj4sg" data-start="1753" data-end="1769">Core palette</h3>
<p data-start="1770" data-end="1812">From the captures, your brand language is:</p>
<ul data-start="1814" data-end="2093">
<li data-section-id="jnkrck" data-start="1814" data-end="1864">
<p data-start="1816" data-end="1864"><strong data-start="1816" data-end="1835">Deep navy / ink</strong> for authority and discipline</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="26ca2v" data-start="1865" data-end="1900">
<p data-start="1867" data-end="1900"><strong data-start="1867" data-end="1877">Orange</strong> for action and urgency</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="gae2t8" data-start="1901" data-end="1951">
<p data-start="1903" data-end="1951"><strong data-start="1903" data-end="1927">Electric blue / cyan</strong> for technical modernity</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="iwzo5e" data-start="1952" data-end="1993">
<p data-start="1954" data-end="1993"><strong data-start="1954" data-end="1962">Teal</strong> for status/progress/completion</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1212isb" data-start="1994" data-end="2054">
<p data-start="1996" data-end="2054"><strong data-start="1996" data-end="2022">Light gray / off-white</strong> for breathable content sections</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="h5rikq" data-start="2055" data-end="2093">
<p data-start="2057" data-end="2093"><strong data-start="2057" data-end="2079">Blue-black / slate</strong> for body text</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2095" data-end="2134">A practical working token set would be:</p>
<div class="TyagGW_tableContainer"><div tabindex="-1" class="group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit"><table data-start="2136" data-end="2788" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="2136" data-end="2166"><tr data-start="2136" data-end="2166"><th data-start="2136" data-end="2144" data-col-size="sm" class="">Token</th><th data-start="2144" data-end="2159" data-col-size="sm" class="" style="text-align: right;">Approx value</th><th data-start="2159" data-end="2166" data-col-size="sm" class="">Use</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2182" data-end="2788"><tr data-start="2182" data-end="2237"><td data-start="2182" data-end="2197" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2184" data-end="2196">--navy-950</code></td><td data-start="2197" data-end="2209" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2199" data-end="2208">#121A2F</code></td><td data-start="2209" data-end="2237" data-col-size="sm">primary dark backgrounds</td></tr><tr data-start="2238" data-end="2292"><td data-start="2238" data-end="2253" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2240" data-end="2252">--navy-900</code></td><td data-start="2253" data-end="2265" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2255" data-end="2264">#18233A</code></td><td data-start="2265" data-end="2292" data-col-size="sm">cards / header / footer</td></tr><tr data-start="2293" data-end="2347"><td data-start="2293" data-end="2308" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2295" data-end="2307">--navy-800</code></td><td data-start="2308" data-end="2320" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2310" data-end="2319">#22314A</code></td><td data-start="2320" data-end="2347" data-col-size="sm">secondary dark surfaces</td></tr><tr data-start="2348" data-end="2408"><td data-start="2348" data-end="2363" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2350" data-end="2362">--blue-500</code></td><td data-start="2363" data-end="2375" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2365" data-end="2374">#2E9BFF</code></td><td data-start="2375" data-end="2408" data-col-size="sm">technical accent / highlights</td></tr><tr data-start="2409" data-end="2456"><td data-start="2409" data-end="2424" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2411" data-end="2423">--cyan-500</code></td><td data-start="2424" data-end="2436" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2426" data-end="2435">#23B6D6</code></td><td data-start="2436" data-end="2456" data-col-size="sm">secondary accent</td></tr><tr data-start="2457" data-end="2515"><td data-start="2457" data-end="2472" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2459" data-end="2471">--teal-500</code></td><td data-start="2472" data-end="2484" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2474" data-end="2483">#2FC6B4</code></td><td data-start="2484" data-end="2515" data-col-size="sm">completion / project status</td></tr><tr data-start="2516" data-end="2562"><td data-start="2516" data-end="2533" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2518" data-end="2532">--orange-500</code></td><td data-start="2533" data-end="2545" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2535" data-end="2544">#F47B20</code></td><td data-start="2545" data-end="2562" data-col-size="sm">CTA / urgency</td></tr><tr data-start="2563" data-end="2615"><td data-start="2563" data-end="2580" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2565" data-end="2579">--orange-600</code></td><td data-start="2580" data-end="2592" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2582" data-end="2591">#E56F16</code></td><td data-start="2592" data-end="2615" data-col-size="sm">hover / pressed CTA</td></tr><tr data-start="2616" data-end="2659"><td data-start="2616" data-end="2628" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2618" data-end="2627">--bg-50</code></td><td data-start="2628" data-end="2640" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2630" data-end="2639">#F6F8FA</code></td><td data-start="2640" data-end="2659" data-col-size="sm">page background</td></tr><tr data-start="2660" data-end="2699"><td data-start="2660" data-end="2675" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2662" data-end="2674">--text-900</code></td><td data-start="2675" data-end="2687" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2677" data-end="2686">#182238</code></td><td data-start="2687" data-end="2699" data-col-size="sm">headings</td></tr><tr data-start="2700" data-end="2740"><td data-start="2700" data-end="2715" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2702" data-end="2714">--text-600</code></td><td data-start="2715" data-end="2727" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2717" data-end="2726">#66748B</code></td><td data-start="2727" data-end="2740" data-col-size="sm">body copy</td></tr><tr data-start="2741" data-end="2788"><td data-start="2741" data-end="2758" data-col-size="sm"><code data-start="2743" data-end="2757">--border-200</code></td><td data-start="2758" data-end="2770" data-col-size="sm" style="text-align: right;"><code data-start="2760" data-end="2769">#D7DFE8</code></td><td data-start="2770" data-end="2788" data-col-size="sm">subtle borders</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 32.6562px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<h3 data-section-id="w7r6s7" data-start="2790" data-end="2814">Brand interpretation</h3>
<p data-start="2815" data-end="2834">The brand reads as:</p>
<ul data-start="2835" data-end="2960">
<li data-section-id="187phei" data-start="2835" data-end="2845">
<p data-start="2837" data-end="2845">credible</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ha7xn0" data-start="2846" data-end="2867">
<p data-start="2848" data-end="2867">regionally grounded</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15uaslt" data-start="2868" data-end="2891">
<p data-start="2870" data-end="2891">technically competent</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="r9bdzo" data-start="2892" data-end="2904">
<p data-start="2894" data-end="2904">not flashy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="wxnt9e" data-start="2905" data-end="2960">
<p data-start="2907" data-end="2960">construction-professional rather than agency-polished</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2962" data-end="2993">That is correct for your buyer.</p>
<hr data-start="2995" data-end="2998">
<h2 data-section-id="44tg4z" data-start="3000" data-end="3069">2. Current homepage: what it does well, and where it underperforms</h2>
<h3 data-section-id="ebuutf" data-start="3071" data-end="3097">What is already strong</h3>
<p data-start="3098" data-end="3149">The current and redesign directions already convey:</p>
<ul data-start="3151" data-end="3331">
<li data-section-id="b9416s" data-start="3151" data-end="3171">
<p data-start="3153" data-end="3171">Bay Area relevance</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1je0bfm" data-start="3172" data-end="3201">
<p data-start="3174" data-end="3201">technical + field crossover</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1u9i89r" data-start="3202" data-end="3228">
<p data-start="3204" data-end="3228">broad service capability</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1k31nbk" data-start="3229" data-end="3266">
<p data-start="3231" data-end="3266">a credible dark/light visual rhythm</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="10b4e5y" data-start="3267" data-end="3303">
<p data-start="3269" data-end="3303">good use of actual project imagery</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="n8cyxe" data-start="3304" data-end="3331">
<p data-start="3306" data-end="3331">strong CTA color contrast</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="17bqetg" data-start="3333" data-end="3369">Where the homepage underperforms</h3>
<p data-start="3370" data-end="3487">The homepage is still a bit slow to answer the first five questions a GC, superintendent, architect, or engineer has:</p>
<ol data-start="3489" data-end="3717">
<li data-section-id="qtvugx" data-start="3489" data-end="3530">
<p data-start="3492" data-end="3530"><strong data-start="3492" data-end="3530">Can these people actually execute?</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="s39tkj" data-start="3531" data-end="3589">
<p data-start="3534" data-end="3589"><strong data-start="3534" data-end="3589">Do they know this jurisdiction and project reality?</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="akrw75" data-start="3590" data-end="3637">
<p data-start="3593" data-end="3637"><strong data-start="3593" data-end="3637">What kind of jobs have they done nearby?</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="13vjd7c" data-start="3638" data-end="3684">
<p data-start="3641" data-end="3684"><strong data-start="3641" data-end="3684">Will they reduce friction or create it?</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1jkaute" data-start="3685" data-end="3717">
<p data-start="3688" data-end="3717"><strong data-start="3688" data-end="3717">Who exactly are they for?</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="3719" data-end="3809">Right now, some of the strongest trust material is present, but too far down or too broad.</p>
<hr data-start="3811" data-end="3814">
<h2 data-section-id="ng0j38" data-start="3816" data-end="3849">3. Best homepage re-sequencing</h2>
<p data-start="3850" data-end="3920">You were right to frame this as a <strong data-start="3884" data-end="3902">reorganization</strong>, not an overhaul.</p>
<p data-start="3922" data-end="3952">The correct homepage order is:</p>
<h3 data-section-id="gzf3t" data-start="3954" data-end="3965">A. Hero</h3>
<p data-start="3966" data-end="4035">Keep the hero concept. Tighten copy if needed, but do not blow it up.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="5mrmll" data-start="4037" data-end="4064">B. Immediate proof rail</h3>
<p data-start="4065" data-end="4138">Add this directly under the hero. This is your single highest-value move.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1pogdik" data-start="4140" data-end="4171">C. Core capability snapshot</h3>
<p data-start="4172" data-end="4220">Keep the capability cards, but sharpen the copy.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="aqz3w" data-start="4222" data-end="4261">D. Condensed project evidence block</h3>
<p data-start="4262" data-end="4328">This is where your <strong data-start="4281" data-end="4319">rotating snippet + interactive map</strong> belongs.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1ez5uy3" data-start="4330" data-end="4357">E. Relevant work teaser</h3>
<p data-start="4358" data-end="4377">Show 4–6 cards max.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="10kuttm" data-start="4379" data-end="4408">F. Delivery/process strip</h3>
<p data-start="4409" data-end="4468">Your “How We Deliver” style section is useful and on-brand.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="c8yxh8" data-start="4470" data-end="4500">G. Team credibility teaser</h3>
<p data-start="4501" data-end="4555">Not the entire team grid. Just enough to signal depth.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="mluk7u" data-start="4557" data-end="4585">H. One testimonial block</h3>
<p data-start="4586" data-end="4621">Support proof; do not lead with it.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1671hfd" data-start="4623" data-end="4651">I. Inquiry / contact CTA</h3>
<p data-start="4652" data-end="4675">Keep strong and direct.</p>
<hr data-start="4677" data-end="4680">
<h1 data-section-id="1lubfj1" data-start="4682" data-end="4725">4. Component-by-component recommendations</h1>
<h2 data-section-id="za5t67" data-start="4727" data-end="4751">Proof rail under hero</h2>
<p data-start="4752" data-end="4806">This should be <strong data-start="4767" data-end="4805">compact, horizontal, and immediate</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="4808" data-end="4866">Do not make it a large card section. Make it a trust band.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="13hb7sj" data-start="4868" data-end="4881">Structure</h3>
<p data-start="4882" data-end="4896">Use 5–6 items:</p>
<ul data-start="4898" data-end="5098">
<li data-section-id="mpplfs" data-start="4898" data-end="4929">
<p data-start="4900" data-end="4929">40+ years Bay Area experience</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="14wv3ac" data-start="4930" data-end="4970">
<p data-start="4932" data-end="4970">In-house engineering + field execution</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ftzzsl" data-start="4971" data-end="4993">
<p data-start="4973" data-end="4993">Class A / B licensed</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1fjdzt2" data-start="4994" data-end="5018">
<p data-start="4996" data-end="5018">PE / QSD / QSP support</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="gsryog" data-start="5019" data-end="5055">
<p data-start="5021" data-end="5055">Public works + commercial delivery</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1v20vw" data-start="5056" data-end="5098">
<p data-start="5058" data-end="5098">Inspection, compliance, closeout support</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1dz3o8e" data-start="5100" data-end="5120">Why this matters</h3>
<p data-start="5121" data-end="5224">This audience scans. They do not want to infer competence from brand mood. They want competence stated.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="eadtfm" data-start="5226" data-end="5245">Design guidance</h3>
<ul data-start="5246" data-end="5398">
<li data-section-id="qbxn8e" data-start="5246" data-end="5279">
<p data-start="5248" data-end="5279">one-row desktop, two-row mobile</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1j79u7p" data-start="5280" data-end="5321">
<p data-start="5282" data-end="5321">muted icon + bold label + short subline</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="rtbl09" data-start="5322" data-end="5335">
<p data-start="5324" data-end="5335">no carousel</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="slov7h" data-start="5336" data-end="5355">
<p data-start="5338" data-end="5355">minimal animation</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1rneoxh" data-start="5356" data-end="5398">
<p data-start="5358" data-end="5398">light section background under dark hero</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="5400" data-end="5403">
<h2 data-section-id="1tvqo3l" data-start="5405" data-end="5448">Condensed rotating project snippet + map</h2>
<p data-start="5449" data-end="5492">This is the second most important addition.</p>
<p data-start="5494" data-end="5582">The homepage version should be a <strong data-start="5527" data-end="5553">condensed proof module</strong>, not a full project browser.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="10o2cem" data-start="5584" data-end="5602">Desktop layout</h3>
<ul data-start="5603" data-end="5699">
<li data-section-id="pekg1p" data-start="5603" data-end="5652">
<p data-start="5605" data-end="5652"><strong data-start="5605" data-end="5621">Left column:</strong> rotating project snippet stack</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1fgj4l8" data-start="5653" data-end="5699">
<p data-start="5655" data-end="5699"><strong data-start="5655" data-end="5672">Right column:</strong> simplified interactive map</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1iazdai" data-start="5701" data-end="5720">Snippet content</h3>
<p data-start="5721" data-end="5743">Each item should show:</p>
<ul data-start="5745" data-end="5820">
<li data-section-id="1hvdobh" data-start="5745" data-end="5760">
<p data-start="5747" data-end="5760">project title</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="whxzxx" data-start="5761" data-end="5771">
<p data-start="5763" data-end="5771">location</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="lz7h6t" data-start="5772" data-end="5790">
<p data-start="5774" data-end="5790">service category</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1lpej18" data-start="5791" data-end="5799">
<p data-start="5793" data-end="5799">status</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="by6gh5" data-start="5800" data-end="5820">
<p data-start="5802" data-end="5820">one proof sentence</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5822" data-end="5830">Example:</p>
<ul data-start="5831" data-end="5979">
<li data-section-id="wxj3vz" data-start="5831" data-end="5873">
<p data-start="5833" data-end="5873"><strong data-start="5833" data-end="5873">Seismic Retrofit — Parking Structure</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1q6yex5" data-start="5874" data-end="5888">
<p data-start="5876" data-end="5888">San Jose, CA</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="117mrvz" data-start="5889" data-end="5905">
<p data-start="5891" data-end="5905">Infrastructure</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1bhuqfc" data-start="5906" data-end="5927">
<p data-start="5908" data-end="5927">Active-site phasing</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="uv9hs3" data-start="5928" data-end="5979">
<p data-start="5930" data-end="5979">Kept the structure partially open during delivery</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="7tpncm" data-start="5981" data-end="5997">Map behavior</h3>
<ul data-start="5998" data-end="6153">
<li data-section-id="4609vz" data-start="5998" data-end="6046">
<p data-start="6000" data-end="6046">active snippet highlights corresponding marker</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1hbulpq" data-start="6047" data-end="6080">
<p data-start="6049" data-end="6080">hovering a marker swaps snippet</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1i5vs6y" data-start="6081" data-end="6116">
<p data-start="6083" data-end="6116">5–8 curated projects only on home</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="sj7sy" data-start="6117" data-end="6153">
<p data-start="6119" data-end="6153">CTA: “View all project experience”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="i9segg" data-start="6155" data-end="6186">What not to include on home</h3>
<p data-start="6187" data-end="6314">Do not bring the full county panel, full service filter set, or the full map/list application to the homepage. That belongs on:</p>
<ul data-start="6315" data-end="6361">
<li data-section-id="1bzzafp" data-start="6315" data-end="6332">
<p data-start="6317" data-end="6332">Project Gallery</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="16yqhhh" data-start="6333" data-end="6340">
<p data-start="6335" data-end="6340">About</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="3mbe8h" data-start="6341" data-end="6361">
<p data-start="6343" data-end="6361">Contact / Estimate</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="6363" data-end="6366">
<h2 data-section-id="1tfriyr" data-start="6368" data-end="6391">Relevant work teaser</h2>
<p data-start="6392" data-end="6435">Your gallery card language is already good.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="4g71s7" data-start="6437" data-end="6458">Keep on each card</h3>
<ul data-start="6459" data-end="6499">
<li data-section-id="162o05r" data-start="6459" data-end="6466">
<p data-start="6461" data-end="6466">image</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15j8uw7" data-start="6467" data-end="6480">
<p data-start="6469" data-end="6480">service tag</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="16mm694" data-start="6481" data-end="6488">
<p data-start="6483" data-end="6488">title</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="whxzxx" data-start="6489" data-end="6499">
<p data-start="6491" data-end="6499">location</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1krh5im" data-start="6501" data-end="6519">Remove on home</h3>
<ul data-start="6520" data-end="6612">
<li data-section-id="1yn8qhu" data-start="6520" data-end="6539">
<p data-start="6522" data-end="6539">too much metadata</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1qk2zo4" data-start="6540" data-end="6558">
<p data-start="6542" data-end="6558">too many filters</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1xrxh0w" data-start="6559" data-end="6612">
<p data-start="6561" data-end="6612">anything that turns it into a tool instead of proof</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6614" data-end="6647">Use 4–6 cards and one strong CTA.</p>
<hr data-start="6649" data-end="6652">
<h2 data-section-id="1b6jh0o" data-start="6654" data-end="6675">Testimonial module</h2>
<p data-start="6676" data-end="6757">The testimonial design is visually solid, but it is not your first trust-builder.</p>
<p data-start="6759" data-end="6799">For this market, testimonials should be:</p>
<ul data-start="6800" data-end="6846">
<li data-section-id="16nbfkq" data-start="6800" data-end="6807">
<p data-start="6802" data-end="6807">short</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="123r1ew" data-start="6808" data-end="6818">
<p data-start="6810" data-end="6818">specific</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="uzlnmb" data-start="6819" data-end="6846">
<p data-start="6821" data-end="6846">tied to operational proof</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6848" data-end="7044">The strongest testimonial in your attachments is strong because it references <strong data-start="6926" data-end="6972">keeping a parking structure partially open</strong> and <strong data-start="6977" data-end="7003">zero full-closure days</strong>. That is the right kind of social proof.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1oqyx9r" data-start="7046" data-end="7064">Recommendation</h3>
<p data-start="7065" data-end="7138">Use one testimonial on home, lower on page.<br>
Use the full rotating set on:</p>
<ul data-start="7139" data-end="7174">
<li data-section-id="16yqhhh" data-start="7139" data-end="7146">
<p data-start="7141" data-end="7146">About</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1bzzafp" data-start="7147" data-end="7164">
<p data-start="7149" data-end="7164">Project Gallery</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="60qq3s" data-start="7165" data-end="7174">
<p data-start="7167" data-end="7174">Contact</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="7176" data-end="7179">
<h2 data-section-id="dz2k9d" data-start="7181" data-end="7221">Preliminary estimate / scoped inquiry</h2>
<p data-start="7222" data-end="7283">This is useful, but not as a first-wave homepage centerpiece.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="rz34gs" data-start="7285" data-end="7306">Best role on home</h3>
<ul data-start="7307" data-end="7372">
<li data-section-id="ukqnm8" data-start="7307" data-end="7330">
<p data-start="7309" data-end="7330">teaser or compact CTA</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="mptthr" data-start="7331" data-end="7372">
<p data-start="7333" data-end="7372">not the primary interaction surface yet</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="fea7sl" data-start="7374" data-end="7388">Better use</h3>
<p data-start="7389" data-end="7417">Use the fuller estimator on:</p>
<ul data-start="7418" data-end="7461">
<li data-section-id="60qq3s" data-start="7418" data-end="7427">
<p data-start="7420" data-end="7427">Contact</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="7ce1zy" data-start="7428" data-end="7438">
<p data-start="7430" data-end="7438">Estimate</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="it9rsx" data-start="7439" data-end="7461">
<p data-start="7441" data-end="7461">Project intake pages</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="7463" data-end="7466">
<h2 data-section-id="1b14shd" data-start="7468" data-end="7483">Team section</h2>
<p data-start="7484" data-end="7541">The full expert grid is credible, but too heavy for home.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1uxtpb7" data-start="7543" data-end="7566">Better home version</h3>
<p data-start="7567" data-end="7588">Feature 3 people max:</p>
<ul data-start="7589" data-end="7699">
<li data-section-id="fsmf07" data-start="7589" data-end="7621">
<p data-start="7591" data-end="7621">principal / engineering leader</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="jf3ahy" data-start="7622" data-end="7658">
<p data-start="7624" data-end="7658">field / superintendent / estimator</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="jggqbb" data-start="7659" data-end="7699">
<p data-start="7661" data-end="7699">inspection / geology / compliance lead</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="7701" data-end="7766">This tells the buyer there are real operators behind the company.</p>
<hr data-start="7768" data-end="7771">
<h1 data-section-id="163ir99" data-start="7773" data-end="7820">5. Messaging strategy for your exact audience</h1>
<p data-start="7822" data-end="7897">Your buyers are not generic “visitors.” They are risk managers in disguise.</p>
<p data-start="7899" data-end="7942">That means your homepage copy should favor:</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1oyu2ef" data-start="7944" data-end="7959">Good themes</h3>
<ul data-start="7960" data-end="8197">
<li data-section-id="1s4oqv3" data-start="7960" data-end="7978">
<p data-start="7962" data-end="7978">constructability</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="164qc1c" data-start="7979" data-end="8000">
<p data-start="7981" data-end="8000">permit coordination</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="17p2sqn" data-start="8001" data-end="8018">
<p data-start="8003" data-end="8018">phased delivery</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="bsiaqq" data-start="8019" data-end="8043">
<p data-start="8021" data-end="8043">closeout documentation</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="arvnt3" data-start="8044" data-end="8071">
<p data-start="8046" data-end="8071">Bay Area field conditions</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="kkumwa" data-start="8072" data-end="8098">
<p data-start="8074" data-end="8098">public works familiarity</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="nqci3r" data-start="8099" data-end="8139">
<p data-start="8101" data-end="8139">inspection / compliance accountability</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="30hk7k" data-start="8140" data-end="8170">
<p data-start="8142" data-end="8170">in-house engineering support</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="omywyj" data-start="8171" data-end="8197">
<p data-start="8173" data-end="8197">reduced project friction</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1fzx54t" data-start="8199" data-end="8221">Avoid leading with</h3>
<ul data-start="8222" data-end="8348">
<li data-section-id="oa5czw" data-start="8222" data-end="8249">
<p data-start="8224" data-end="8249">vague excellence language</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="kbe53a" data-start="8250" data-end="8279">
<p data-start="8252" data-end="8279">generic innovation language</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="y2oycp" data-start="8280" data-end="8314">
<p data-start="8282" data-end="8314">broad “we build dreams” language</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15g4qsc" data-start="8315" data-end="8348">
<p data-start="8317" data-end="8348">overly polished agency phrasing</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8350" data-end="8475">The PDF’s strongest messaging is strong because it sounds operational, not promotional. <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_2ju_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span></p>
<hr data-start="8477" data-end="8480">
<h1 data-section-id="1v73zwk" data-start="8482" data-end="8505">6. Monorepo trim plan</h1>
<p data-start="8506" data-end="8663">I still have not been able to read the actual repo tree or files, so I will not pretend I have. But I can give you the <strong data-start="8625" data-end="8649">correct target shape</strong> for trimming.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="apztd9" data-start="8665" data-end="8683">Target topology</h2>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="8685" data-end="9038"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy"><div class="cm-scroller"><div class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly"><span>apps/</span><br><span>  marketing-site/</span><br><span>  internal-portal/</span><br><span>  client-portal/</span><br><br><span>services/</span><br><span>  marketing-api/</span><br><span>  internal-api/</span><br><span>  client-api/</span><br><br><span>packages/</span><br><span>  brand-tokens/</span><br><span>  ui-marketing/</span><br><span>  ui-portal/</span><br><span>  forms/</span><br><span>  maps/</span><br><span>  auth/</span><br><span>  shared-types/</span><br><span>  shared-utils/</span><br><br><span>content/</span><br><span>  marketing/</span><br><span>  case-studies/</span><br><span>  resources/</span><br><br><span>docs/</span><br><span>  architecture/</span><br><span>  product/</span><br><span>  operations/</span><br><span>  archive/</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<h2 data-section-id="1uyd9fl" data-start="9040" data-end="9086">What should probably be removed or archived</h2>
<p data-start="9087" data-end="9135">When I can inspect the repo, I will look to cut:</p>
<ul data-start="9137" data-end="9494">
<li data-section-id="g5lznh" data-start="9137" data-end="9159">
<p data-start="9139" data-end="9159">abandoned prototypes</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="gffdtj" data-start="9160" data-end="9183">
<p data-start="9162" data-end="9183">duplicated app shells</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1iiqg77" data-start="9184" data-end="9200">
<p data-start="9186" data-end="9200">backup folders</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1p4qbti" data-start="9201" data-end="9255">
<p data-start="9203" data-end="9255">legacy screenshots/assets mixed into runtime folders</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="9cfsh5" data-start="9256" data-end="9287">
<p data-start="9258" data-end="9287">duplicate component libraries</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="tf0dxi" data-start="9288" data-end="9310">
<p data-start="9290" data-end="9310">dead API experiments</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="14j3qil" data-start="9311" data-end="9334">
<p data-start="9313" data-end="9334">duplicated auth logic</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1vnmjq3" data-start="9335" data-end="9401">
<p data-start="9337" data-end="9401">one-off admin tools not tied to internal portal or client portal</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="npy9n1" data-start="9402" data-end="9422">
<p data-start="9404" data-end="9422">stale demo content</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1f6eeco" data-start="9423" data-end="9445">
<p data-start="9425" data-end="9445">old migration debris</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1h62hdq" data-start="9446" data-end="9494">
<p data-start="9448" data-end="9494">orphaned package managers / lockfile conflicts</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="gm8vyb" data-start="9496" data-end="9525">Rule for keeping something</h2>
<p data-start="9526" data-end="9608">A package, folder, or document should stay only if it clearly serves one of these:</p>
<ul data-start="9610" data-end="9722">
<li data-section-id="1ms5ax3" data-start="9610" data-end="9626">
<p data-start="9612" data-end="9626">marketing site</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="7if9az" data-start="9627" data-end="9644">
<p data-start="9629" data-end="9644">internal portal</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="9cxzlx" data-start="9645" data-end="9660">
<p data-start="9647" data-end="9660">client portal</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="8fmz00" data-start="9661" data-end="9684">
<p data-start="9663" data-end="9684">one of their backends</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="lf2z1e" data-start="9685" data-end="9722">
<p data-start="9687" data-end="9722">a truly shared package between them</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="9724" data-end="9780">If not, it should move to <code data-start="9750" data-end="9765">docs/archive/</code> or be deleted.</p>
<hr data-start="9782" data-end="9785">
<h1 data-section-id="1tznji3" data-start="9787" data-end="9825">7. Figma: how I would use it for you</h1>
<p data-start="9826" data-end="9865">I can use your Figma account from here.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="9jz5fh" data-start="9867" data-end="9897">Best use of Figma right now</h2>
<p data-start="9898" data-end="9931">Not full-page redesigns. Instead:</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1ok5pet" data-start="9933" data-end="9967">First-wave components to build</h3>
<ol data-start="9968" data-end="10181">
<li data-section-id="xuxlg8" data-start="9968" data-end="9990">
<p data-start="9971" data-end="9990"><strong data-start="9971" data-end="9990">Hero proof rail</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1u0hhon" data-start="9991" data-end="10045">
<p data-start="9994" data-end="10045"><strong data-start="9994" data-end="10045">Condensed project map + rotating snippet module</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="wj34k8" data-start="10046" data-end="10078">
<p data-start="10049" data-end="10078"><strong data-start="10049" data-end="10078">Featured work card system</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="xajplq" data-start="10079" data-end="10108">
<p data-start="10082" data-end="10108"><strong data-start="10082" data-end="10108">Small team proof cards</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="jwobpc" data-start="10109" data-end="10133">
<p data-start="10112" data-end="10133"><strong data-start="10112" data-end="10133">Testimonial block</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1h1npnc" data-start="10134" data-end="10181">
<p data-start="10137" data-end="10181"><strong data-start="10137" data-end="10181">Project-intake teaser / estimator teaser</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 data-section-id="1refq38" data-start="10183" data-end="10221">Figma-community adaptation approach</h2>
<p data-start="10222" data-end="10380">If you want me to adapt community patterns, I would use community inspiration only for <strong data-start="10309" data-end="10338">interaction and structure</strong>, then restyle them fully into your brand:</p>
<ul data-start="10382" data-end="10567">
<li data-section-id="1e24f76" data-start="10382" data-end="10417">
<p data-start="10384" data-end="10417">darker, more disciplined surfaces</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1cbt631" data-start="10418" data-end="10436">
<p data-start="10420" data-end="10436">stronger spacing</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="vnukib" data-start="10437" data-end="10456">
<p data-start="10439" data-end="10456">restrained motion</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="syrnc1" data-start="10457" data-end="10482">
<p data-start="10459" data-end="10482">operational iconography</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="rqs3sx" data-start="10483" data-end="10531">
<p data-start="10485" data-end="10531">construction/professional typography hierarchy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="mc72bu" data-start="10532" data-end="10567">
<p data-start="10534" data-end="10567">your navy/orange/cyan/teal system</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="17dal64" data-start="10569" data-end="10611">What I would avoid in community imports</h2>
<ul data-start="10612" data-end="10763">
<li data-section-id="dkdshw" data-start="10612" data-end="10632">
<p data-start="10614" data-end="10632">startup-SaaS gloss</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="a6ytnx" data-start="10633" data-end="10658">
<p data-start="10635" data-end="10658">soft consumer gradients</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="pc6zvg" data-start="10659" data-end="10687">
<p data-start="10661" data-end="10687">oversized neumorphic cards</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="n16qwk" data-start="10688" data-end="10711">
<p data-start="10690" data-end="10711">playful illustrations</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="nwat0j" data-start="10712" data-end="10738">
<p data-start="10714" data-end="10738">over-animated dashboards</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="d53dd2" data-start="10739" data-end="10763">
<p data-start="10741" data-end="10763">generic CRM aesthetics</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="10765" data-end="10768">
<h1 data-section-id="5jbbin" data-start="10770" data-end="10803">8. My strongest recommendations</h1>
<h2 data-section-id="1mtyyme" data-start="10805" data-end="10838">Highest-value homepage changes</h2>
<ol data-start="10839" data-end="11119">
<li data-section-id="cdvd3y" data-start="10839" data-end="10885">
<p data-start="10842" data-end="10885">Add the <strong data-start="10850" data-end="10864">proof rail</strong> directly under hero.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1b02lhd" data-start="10886" data-end="10977">
<p data-start="10889" data-end="10977">Add the <strong data-start="10897" data-end="10933">condensed rotating project + map</strong> block above the fold-adjacent content area.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="d3y5tt" data-start="10978" data-end="11025">
<p data-start="10981" data-end="11025">Reduce the home-page map/gallery complexity.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="l19gnu" data-start="11026" data-end="11074">
<p data-start="11029" data-end="11074">Use one strong testimonial lower on the page.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="zr6gvh" data-start="11075" data-end="11119">
<p data-start="11078" data-end="11119">Keep the contact block strong and simple.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 data-section-id="g9wsfn" data-start="11121" data-end="11153">Highest-value content changes</h2>
<ol data-start="11154" data-end="11415">
<li data-section-id="t922bg" data-start="11154" data-end="11202">
<p data-start="11157" data-end="11202">Rewrite headings for operational credibility.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1fvderb" data-start="11203" data-end="11249">
<p data-start="11206" data-end="11249">Make project proof more local and specific.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="4wrhx0" data-start="11250" data-end="11323">
<p data-start="11253" data-end="11323">Use more “field reality / phasing / permitting / compliance” language.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1uyb2dp" data-start="11324" data-end="11415">
<p data-start="11327" data-end="11415">Make the audience feel understood without explicitly naming every trade role everywhere.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 data-section-id="bbtefm" data-start="11417" data-end="11446">Highest-value repo changes</h2>
<ol data-start="11447" data-end="11710">
<li data-section-id="1qq25xw" data-start="11447" data-end="11496">
<p data-start="11450" data-end="11496">Separate deployable apps from shared packages.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1qhmt4z" data-start="11497" data-end="11544">
<p data-start="11500" data-end="11544">Archive or delete prototypes and duplicates.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="87hdup" data-start="11545" data-end="11597">
<p data-start="11548" data-end="11597">Isolate marketing content/data from portal logic.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1rupfwe" data-start="11598" data-end="11658">
<p data-start="11601" data-end="11658">Normalize UI libraries into marketing vs portal surfaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1gael78" data-start="11659" data-end="11710">
<p data-start="11662" data-end="11710">Cut dead weight before trying to scale features.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="11712" data-end="11715">
<h1 data-section-id="oy6ads" data-start="11717" data-end="11740">What is still blocked</h1>
<p data-start="11741" data-end="11920">I still cannot do the <strong data-start="11763" data-end="11788">actual repo deep read</strong> because the GitHub search connector in this chat has no selected repository. The exact error is still <code data-start="11891" data-end="11919">MissingGithubRepoSelection</code>.</p>
<p data-start="11922" data-end="11951">To unblock that in this chat:</p>
<ul data-start="11952" data-end="12032">
<li data-section-id="18ziiet" data-start="11952" data-end="11968">
<p data-start="11954" data-end="11968">type <code data-start="11959" data-end="11968">@github</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="vz0jpt" data-start="11969" data-end="11996">
<p data-start="11971" data-end="11996">click the <strong data-start="11981" data-end="11991">GitHub</strong> icon</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="n0ljp5" data-start="11997" data-end="12032">
<p data-start="11999" data-end="12032">select <code data-start="12006" data-end="12032">dylanlmeraki/last_breath</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="12034" data-end="12114">Once that is done, I can use the uploaded <code data-start="12076" data-end="12096">github-repo-reader</code> skill process to:</p>
<ul data-start="12115" data-end="12371">
<li data-section-id="1m53u20" data-start="12115" data-end="12146">
<p data-start="12117" data-end="12146">materialize the repo snapshot</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1lduwi0" data-start="12147" data-end="12172">
<p data-start="12149" data-end="12172">map the actual monorepo</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="fjmns" data-start="12173" data-end="12219">
<p data-start="12175" data-end="12219">identify dead folders and redundant packages</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1a2fj" data-start="12220" data-end="12249">
<p data-start="12222" data-end="12249">propose the exact trim plan</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1mnakrm" data-start="12250" data-end="12306">
<p data-start="12252" data-end="12306">map the marketing site’s actual component entry points</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="xci59e" data-start="12307" data-end="12371">
<p data-start="12309" data-end="12371">give you a grounded integration plan against the real codebase</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="12373" data-end="12483" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">After you select the repo here, send <code data-start="12410" data-end="12414">go</code> and I’ll do the repo-level pass plus the first Figma component plan.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="relative h-[60px] select-none"><div class="absolute h-[60px]" style="opacity: 1;"><button class="not-prose group/footnote border-token-border-default bg-token-main-surface-primary hover:bg-token-main-surface-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 mt-3 mb-2 flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl border py-2 ps-3 pe-2.5"><div class="text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-0.5 text-xs font-semibold">Sources</div></button></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div aria-label="Response actions" class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" role="group" tabindex="-1" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy response" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span>