ntent-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="d6d2963b-6ca0-4eed-bf81-9300bea24c32" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><button class="text-token-text-tertiary mx-2 mb-1 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm font-normal focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-current hover:text-token-text-primary mt-1 justify-end" type="button"><span aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#e04414" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span><p class="line-clamp-3">Back to the repo and site
=========================

Now that the repo is indexed, the important structural conclusion stands:

1\. The codebase is one application carrying three products
-----------------------------------------------------------

It is not a true workspace-style monorepo. The root app lazy-loads `InternalApp`, `ClientApp`, and `MarketingApp`, and switches between them based on hostname or route prefix[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/App.tsx)

[App](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/App.tsx)

. Vite is also configured with a single `client` root and a single `dist/public` build output, which confirms the single-app shape[

vite.config

](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/vite.config.ts). The root package is still one package with one build/dev pipeline, not multiple app packages[

package

](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/package.json).

That matters because the right cleanup is **not** “convert to a formal monorepo first.”  
The right cleanup is **trim and isolate scope inside the current app**.

* * *

2\. What to keep, what to park
------------------------------

Keep as active first-class surfaces
-----------------------------------

These are aligned to your stated launch scope:

*   marketing portal
    
*   client portal
    
*   internal portal core ops
    
*   server
    
*   shared
    

The client portal already looks fairly disciplined: auth/register, dashboard, projects, documents, proposals, invoices, messages, reports, RFIs, settings[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/client/ClientApp.tsx)

[ClientApp](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/client/ClientApp.tsx)

.

Park, feature-flag, or move to experimental
-------------------------------------------

The internal portal is the part creating most of the “oversized and disorganized” feeling. It includes core ops plus a large amount of growth/automation/admin tooling such as CRM search, outreach, email sequences, sales bot control, page builder, SEO assistant, content manager, ICP settings, website monitoring, template builder, AI sales assistant, and sequence optimization[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/internal/InternalApp.tsx)

[InternalApp](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/internal/InternalApp.tsx)

.

For your current launch objective, I would classify these as **phase-two or experimental** unless they are already operationally critical:

*   CRM search
    
*   outreach queue
    
*   email sequences
    
*   sequence optimization
    
*   sales bot control
    
*   AI sales assistant
    
*   page builder
    
*   SEO assistant
    
*   content manager
    
*   website monitoring
    
*   ICP settings
    
*   template builder
    

Internal portal core to preserve
--------------------------------

These look much closer to live business value:

*   dashboard
    
*   project manager / project detail / project dashboard
    
*   contacts
    
*   proposals
    
*   invoices
    
*   RFIs
    
*   doc approval
    
*   client communications
    
*   client invites
    
*   user management / profile
    
*   form submissions
    
*   QA/QC, if genuinely used in operations
    

That gives you a much tighter product boundary.

* * *

3\. The homepage issue is sequencing, not visual identity
---------------------------------------------------------

Your current `Home.tsx` is visually strong, but it still behaves like a **brand-first landing page** rather than a **trust-first proof page**.

The file shows a high-investment hero with:

*   video background
    
*   blueprint/grid treatments
    
*   particle field
    
*   floating elements
    
*   scroll progress
    
*   animated transitions and reverse-play video logic[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)
    
    [Home](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)
    

The page already carries the right messages:

*   “Consulting Engineers &amp; Contractors”
    
*   same-day response
    
*   40+ years Bay Area expertise
    
*   SF Bay Area
    
*   licensed PE / QSD / QSP
    
*   Class A &amp; B contractor[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)
    
    [Home](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)
    

That matches the one-pager positioning around construction service, engineering consulting, inspections/testing, stormwater planning, plus field-reality, Bay Area jurisdictional familiarity, and compliance-minded delivery

Union

So the diagnosis is straightforward:

**The messaging is largely correct.  
The order is not yet optimized for your buyer.**

* * *

4\. Exact homepage restructuring I recommend
--------------------------------------------

New order
---------

1.  Hero
    
2.  Proof rail
    
3.  Condensed project proof + map
    
4.  Services snapshot
    
5.  Delivery / “why Pacific”
    
6.  Featured work teaser
    
7.  One testimonial
    
8.  CTA
    

Why
---

Right now, your trust badges appear in the services section instead of immediately under the hero[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

[Home](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

. That means one of your best credibility assets is arriving too late.

For GCs, supers, architects, engineers, and construction professionals, the homepage should answer:

*   Are you qualified?
    
*   Are you local and field-literate?
    
*   What kind of work have you actually done?
    
*   Will you reduce friction?
    
*   Can I get someone on the phone quickly?
    

Your current page answers those, but not in the fastest possible order.

* * *

5\. Exact files I would touch first
-----------------------------------

A. `client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx`
------------------------------------------------

This is the main integration point. It already contains the hero, service intro, trust badges, values, why-choose, and CTA sections[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

[Home](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

### Change

Insert two new sections immediately after the hero:

*   `HomeProofRail`
    
*   `HomeProjectEvidence`
    

Then push the current services section down.

B. `client/src/portals/marketing/marketing.css`
-----------------------------------------------

This file already defines the marketing color variables:

*   `--marketing-primary`
    
*   `--marketing-accent`
    
*   `--marketing-bg`
    
*   `--marketing-cyan`
    
*   `--marketing-orange`[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/marketing.css)
    
    [marketing](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/marketing.css)
    

### Change

Expand this into a fuller token layer so the new homepage modules do not hardcode stylistic decisions inside JSX.

Add:

*   dark navy surface tokens
    
*   light surface tokens
    
*   text tokens
    
*   border tokens
    
*   status tokens for project markers
    

C. Add new component files
--------------------------

I would create:

client/src/portals/marketing/components/HomeProofRail.tsx  
client/src/portals/marketing/components/HomeProjectEvidence.tsx  
client/src/portals/marketing/components/ProjectSnippetRotator.tsx  
client/src/portals/marketing/components/ProjectMiniMap.tsx  
client/src/portals/marketing/data/homeProjectSnippets.ts

That gives you a clean, isolated implementation without destabilizing the rest of marketing.

* * *

6\. Exact component recommendations
-----------------------------------

Proof rail
----------

Take the trust badges that currently sit in the services intro and promote them upward.

Current content already exists in the page:

*   SF Bay Area
    
*   Licensed PE / QSD / QSP
    
*   Class A &amp; B Contractor
    
*   40+ Years[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)
    
    [Home](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)
    

### Convert into a compact proof band

Use 5–6 items:

*   40+ years Bay Area experience
    
*   In-house engineering + field execution
    
*   Licensed PE / QSD / QSP
    
*   Class A &amp; B contractor
    
*   Public works + commercial delivery
    
*   Compliance, inspection, and closeout support
    

### Design rule

Do not make this a large card section.  
Make it a horizontal trust rail.

* * *

Condensed project evidence + map
--------------------------------

This should be your second inserted section.

### Home version only

Show:

*   project title
    
*   city
    
*   discipline
    
*   status
    
*   one proof sentence
    

### Interaction

*   rotating snippet on left
    
*   interactive mini-map on right
    
*   snippet hover updates active marker
    
*   marker hover updates snippet
    

### Keep it small

On home, use only 5–8 curated projects.  
Do not bring the full project-browser complexity into the homepage.

You already have routing in place for a fuller project experience through the marketing app, including `ProjectGallery` and `ProjectDetail`[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/MarketingApp.tsx)

[MarketingApp](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/MarketingApp.tsx)

* * *

7\. Brand/token cleanup
-----------------------

The palette is directionally correct, but the code should be normalized.

Right now, `marketing.css` gives you the basic cyan/orange/slate marketing identity[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/marketing.css)

[marketing](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/marketing.css)

, while the page itself still contains lots of ad hoc gradients and hardcoded visual treatments inside the component tree[

Home

](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx).

### I would formalize these layers

Foundation
----------

*   surface
    
*   text
    
*   border
    
*   shadow
    
*   radius
    
*   spacing
    

Brand
-----

*   navy
    
*   cyan
    
*   orange
    
*   teal
    
*   off-white
    

Status
------

*   active
    
*   completed
    
*   in progress
    
*   warning
    

That matters because the mini-map and project snippet rotator will need status colors, and you do not want those scattered as one-off values through new components.

* * *

8\. How I would use your Figma access
-------------------------------------

The strongest Figma-backed workflow here is:

1.  **Use `figma-internal-scout` logic** to inspect the attached component directions or your live design file
    
2.  **Use `figma-to-code-contract` logic** to define the production-ready props/states/layout invariants for:
    
    *   proof rail
        
    *   project snippet card
        
    *   mini-map
        
    *   featured work card
        
3.  **Use `figma-knowledge-weaver` logic** to write a small `docs/design` knowledge layer in the repo so these choices do not live only in chat
    
4.  **Use `sequential-workbench` logic** to keep the trim and implementation plan disciplined
    

One constraint: although you enabled Figma access, I do not have a Figma Community search tool in this environment. So I can inspect your Figma files directly, but I cannot do a live Figma Community mining pass from here right now.

* * *

9\. My concrete recommendation for the next implementation slice
----------------------------------------------------------------

Do this in order:

Slice 1
-------

Add the proof rail under the hero.

Slice 2
-------

Add the condensed project evidence + mini-map section.

Slice 3
-------

Move the existing trust badges out of the services intro, since they will already be handled above.

Slice 4
-------

Reduce the hero’s motion budget slightly by avoiding further decorative additions there. The hero is already doing enough[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

[Home](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

Slice 5
-------

Park nonessential internal portal modules behind flags or move them into an `experimental` area.

* * *

10\. Blunt summary
------------------

You do **not** need:

*   a homepage overhaul
    
*   a full monorepo rewrite
    
*   a new brand system
    

You **do** need:

