ax-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="5e628a10-3c6d-4a1e-800b-3feecc8ab82c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><button class="text-token-text-tertiary mx-2 mb-1 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm font-normal focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-current hover:text-token-text-primary mt-1 justify-end" type="button"><span aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#e04414" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span><p class="line-clamp-3">Deep advice on brand, voice, and expertise
==========================================

Your market does not reward ornamental confidence. It rewards **operational credibility**.

What your brand voice should sound like
---------------------------------------

*   specific
    
*   field-aware
    
*   permit-aware
    
*   schedule-aware
    
*   compliance-literate
    
*   calm
    
*   technically competent
    
*   regionally grounded
    

What to emphasize more
----------------------

*   Bay Area permitting and agency coordination
    
*   in-house PE / QSD / QSP depth
    
*   self-perform capability where relevant
    
*   constructability
    
*   phased delivery
    
*   stormwater / inspection / documentation discipline
    
*   public works and institutional credibility
    
*   real project scope, not just sector labels
    

What to emphasize less
----------------------

*   abstract innovation language
    
*   startup-style “platform” language on marketing pages
    
*   over-animated hero spectacle
    
*   generic “we build your vision” phrasing
    

Best language pattern
---------------------

Use:

*   **what was done**
    
*   **where**
    
*   **for whom**
    
*   **what risk was handled**
    
*   **what made it credible**
    

That is the best fit for your audience.

* * *

Component folder strategy
=========================

I still recommend these new folders/components:

client/src/portals/marketing/components/  
├── HomeProofRail.tsx  
├── HomeProjectEvidence.tsx  
├── ProjectSnippetRotator.tsx  
├── ProjectMiniMap.tsx  
├── WhyPacific.tsx  
└── FeaturedProjectCards.tsx  
  
client/src/portals/marketing/data/  
├── homeProjectSnippets.ts  
├── projectMarkers.ts  
└── proofRailItems.ts

Layout strategy for each
------------------------

`HomeProofRail.tsx`
-------------------

*   one horizontal band under hero
    
*   6 items desktop
    
*   3x2 tablet
    
*   stacked mobile
    
*   no carousel
    
*   no long copy
    
*   one icon, one value, one support line
    

`HomeProjectEvidence.tsx`
-------------------------

*   section intro on top-left
    
*   snippet rotator left
    
*   map right
    
*   subtle legend
    
*   CTA to full gallery
    
*   keep the home version curated, not filter-heavy
    

`ProjectSnippetRotator.tsx`
---------------------------

*   5–6 curated entries
    
*   active state with slightly stronger border/shadow
    
*   project type pill
    
*   discipline/location/meta line
    
*   proof sentence as the focal content
    

`ProjectMiniMap.tsx`
--------------------

*   not a full GIS tool
    
*   lightweight, high-trust overview
    
*   colored markers by curated status/type
    
*   marker hover syncs with snippet
    

`WhyPacific.tsx`
----------------

Make this more weighted than “how we deliver.”  
Use 3–4 reasons:

*   engineering informed by field reality
    
*   Bay Area jurisdictional familiarity
    
*   compliance-minded documentation
    
*   integrated engineering + construction perspective
    

* * *

Updated part 8 — how I’d use Figma now
======================================

Now that you want the community-miner in the loop, here is the right Figma workflow:

Phase A — internal truth first
------------------------------

Use **figma-internal-scout** against your actual homepage and design file to identify:

*   header/hero spacing rhythm
    
*   card corner/radius system
    
*   section widths
    
*   button families
    
*   current accent usage
    
*   what should be kept vs retired
    

Phase B — targeted community mining
-----------------------------------

Use **figma-community-miner** only for these pattern classes:

*   proof rails
    
*   compact project evidence modules
    
*   mini-map + card sync patterns
    
*   testimonial slider mechanics
    
*   estimator / intake card flow
    

### Rules for community mining

*   mine for structure, not style
    
*   ignore consumer/SaaS gloss
    
*   ignore illustration-heavy patterns
    
*   ignore overly soft card systems
    
*   ignore playful interactions
    

Phase C — contract generation
-----------------------------

Use **figma-to-code-contract** to define:

*   proof rail props/states
    
*   project evidence section layout invariants
    
*   marker/snippet sync behavior
    
*   mobile breakpoints
    
*   card anatomy
    
*   section-specific token usage
    

Phase D — durable memory
------------------------

Use **figma-knowledge-weaver** to preserve:

*   approved homepage order
    
*   approved proof rail copy rules
    
*   approved project snippet field rules
    
*   “Why Pacific” messaging rules
    
*   what stays on home vs what moves to gallery/about/contact
    

Phase E — sequence discipline
-----------------------------

Use **sequential-workbench** to track:

*   homepage changes first
    
*   repo separation later
    
*   internal portal bloat handling later
    
*   gallery/contact/about expansion after home stabilizes
    

### One honest limitation

I attempted a generic Figma search from this environment, but no specific file surfaced from connector search without a direct file or node target. So the workflow above is the correct one, but for file-specific inspection I still want a Figma file URL or node once you want me to canonize a specific layout.

* * *

Updated part 9 — next implementation slices
===========================================

Based on your reply, I would update the sequence to this:

Slice 0 — mental repo separation only
-------------------------------------

Keep the two tree model in working memory.  
Do not refactor yet.

Slice 1 — token cleanup
-----------------------

Replace the current lightweight marketing token layer with a fuller `marketing.css`.  
The existing repo version is still very minimal — mostly a few brand colors and effect helpers[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/marketing.css)

[marketing](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/marketing.css)

Slice 2 — proof rail
--------------------

Add `HomeProofRail` directly under hero.  
Move the current trust badges out of the services intro after that. The current badge set is in the services section now[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

[Home](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx)

Slice 3 — project evidence block
--------------------------------

Add `HomeProjectEvidence` under the proof rail.  
Use the uploaded project materials as the seed source for snippet content and gallery records

example projects completed

example projects completed

Slice 4 — rebalance the mid-page
--------------------------------

Keep services, but give more visual and narrative weight to **Why Pacific Engineering** than to generic delivery language.

Slice 5 — gallery/about/contact expansion
-----------------------------------------

The marketing app already has routes for `about`, `contact`, `project-gallery`, and `project/:slug`[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/MarketingApp.tsx)

[MarketingApp](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/marketing/MarketingApp.tsx)

  
That is where the fuller map, longer project inventory, testimonials, and estimator flow can expand.

Slice 6 — internal cleanup later
--------------------------------

Only after the homepage/marketing side is tighter do we decide what internal items stay active, get feature-flagged, or move into an experimental area. That internal route list is exactly where the bloat pressure is coming from, even though the features are functional[](https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/c94349630a506d05ca4c78125047a483eef63296/client/src/portals/internal/InternalApp.tsx)

