 class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35l_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span></p>
<h3 data-section-id="eykc8v" data-start="2537" data-end="2563">2. Component inventory</h3>
<p data-start="2564" data-end="2924">You are ahead here too. The main site clearly already has the major building blocks: hero, service system, values block, Why Pacific section, CTA, and now—per your Codex state—the proof/evidence components exist and need refinement more than invention. The problem is no longer “missing UI.” It is <strong data-start="2862" data-end="2885">ordering and polish</strong>. <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35m_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Pasted text</p></button></span></p>
<h3 data-section-id="133infq" data-start="2926" data-end="2955">3. Runtime/seam hardening</h3>
<p data-start="2956" data-end="3225">This is farther along than the visual polish work. Your Codex brief says the mid-Phase-4 hardening run is clean for runtime/seam stability, with Playwright matrix, functional flows, and focused loops all passing. That is a strong position to be in before a Monday push.</p>
<hr data-start="3227" data-end="3230">
<h2 data-section-id="1jlkgtv" data-start="3232" data-end="3259">On plan but not finished</h2>
<h3 data-section-id="t03x3z" data-start="3261" data-end="3291">4. Proof/evidence strategy</h3>
<p data-start="3292" data-end="3677">The plan is right and the content is ready, but this area still needs tighter visual execution. The project materials are strong enough to power the homepage and gallery: Port of San Francisco, Caltrans, SFUSD, SFPUC, SFO, and the Chief Medical Examiner Building are all credible, regionally relevant anchors. <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35n_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">example projects completed</p></button></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35o_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">example projects completed</p></button></span></p>
<h3 data-section-id="6iaamd" data-start="3679" data-end="3705">5. Why Pacific section</h3>
<p data-start="3706" data-end="4056">Directionally right, not yet fully mature. The one-pager’s “Why Pacific” logic is still the right strategic base, but this section needs to sound more human and feel less like an intermediate concept block. It should read as refined differentiation, not a draft explanation. <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35p_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35q_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span></p>
<hr data-start="4058" data-end="4061">
<h2 data-section-id="8hl8u2" data-start="4063" data-end="4077">Behind plan</h2>
<h3 data-section-id="aaqm4t" data-start="4079" data-end="4116">6. UX ordering and section rhythm</h3>
<p data-start="4117" data-end="4449">This is still behind. The directly surfaced <code data-start="4161" data-end="4171">Home.tsx</code> snapshot still shows the old sequence and still buries the trust row under services. Even if branch <code data-start="4272" data-end="4284">chillin_v2</code> has progressed since that snapshot, this is still the area you yourself are calling out: spacing and ordering need refinement. <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35r_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Pasted text</p></button></span></p>
<h3 data-section-id="a7p7vj" data-start="4451" data-end="4472">7. Hero restraint</h3>
<p data-start="4473" data-end="4771">Still behind. The verified <code data-start="4500" data-end="4510">Home.tsx</code> snapshot is visually overcommitted at the top: video + multiple overlay systems + particles + floating elements + scroll progress. Even if some of that has been reduced in-branch, this remains the right area to simplify. <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_35s_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Pasted text</p></button></span></p>
<h3 data-section-id="lzn1w" data-start="4773" data-end="4814">8. Palette discipline and color usage</h3>
<p data-start="4815" data-end="5025">Still behind. You already called this out, and it tracks with the earlier state: there is more work to do in making your palette feel governed rather than simply used. This is refinement work, not brand rework.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1gzhzni" data-start="5027" data-end="5052">9. Production imagery</h3>
<p data-start="5053" data-end="5251">Clearly behind. Your Codex brief is explicit: project gallery visuals are still generated, and team/blog/previous-work still use stock or external sources. That is the core remaining gap in Phase 5.</p>
<hr data-start="5253" data-end="5256">
<h1 data-section-id="7fq6kx" data-start="5258" data-end="5293">What this means in plain language</h1>
<p data-start="5295" data-end="5439">You are <strong data-start="5303" data-end="5329">not behind on strategy</strong>.<br data-start="5330" data-end="5333">
You are <strong data-start="5341" data-end="5381">not behind on component availability</strong>.<br data-start="5382" data-end="5385">
You are <strong data-start="5393" data-end="5438">not badly behind on engineering stability</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="5441" data-end="5466">You are mainly behind on:</p>
<ul data-start="5467" data-end="5605">
<li data-section-id="10bdb34" data-start="5467" data-end="5487">
<p data-start="5469" data-end="5487"><strong data-start="5469" data-end="5487">visual editing</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="qvckxb" data-start="5488" data-end="5510">
<p data-start="5490" data-end="5510"><strong data-start="5490" data-end="5510">section ordering</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="140gg2j" data-start="5511" data-end="5531">
<p data-start="5513" data-end="5531"><strong data-start="5513" data-end="5531">spacing rhythm</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="vfg3kv" data-start="5532" data-end="5556">
<p data-start="5534" data-end="5556"><strong data-start="5534" data-end="5556">palette discipline</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1j8zbev" data-start="5557" data-end="5581">
<p data-start="5559" data-end="5581"><strong data-start="5559" data-end="5581">production imagery</strong></p>
</li>
