<h1 data-section-id="1mvtevx" data-start="10627" data-end="10675">Current State Handoff Brief (copy/paste ready)</h1>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="10677" data-end="15434"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="sticky z-2 select-none top-(--sticky-padding-top)"><div class="flex w-full items-center justify-between py-1.5 ps-4 pe-1.5 font-sans md:ps-5 bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary"><div class="flex max-w-[75%] min-w-0 cursor-default items-center text-sm font-medium justify-self-start text-token-text-primary"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-sm me-2.5 shrink-0"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#e45ab3" fill="currentColor"></use></svg>Markdown</div><div class="flex flex-row items-center gap-0.5 justify-self-end"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-4 top-12 bottom-4"><div class="pointer-events-none sticky z-40 shrink-0 z-1!" style="top: calc(calc(var(--sticky-padding-top) + 48px) - 1px * 3); margin-bottom: calc(-4px); height: calc(4px); mask-image: linear-gradient(transparent 25%, white 75%);"><div class="sticky bg-token-border-light" style="top: calc(var(--sticky-padding-top) + 48px); height: 1px;"></div></div></div><div class="relative"><div class="" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy"><div class="cm-scroller"><div class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly"><span># Current State Handoff Brief (Copy/Paste Ready)</span><br><br><span>Branch: `chillin_v2`</span><br><br><span>## Source of truth for current status</span><br><span>Use this handoff plus the latest repo state in `chillin_v2` as truth.</span><br><span>Older chat snapshots of `Home.tsx` may reflect an earlier hero-heavy stage and should be treated as historical UX context, not necessarily current implementation.</span><br><br><span>## Strategic status</span><br><span>The repo is not missing strategy.</span><br><span>It is in a late refinement stage for the marketing site.</span><br><br><span>The strongest areas are:</span><br><span>- brand positioning</span><br><span>- service framing</span><br><span>- trust language</span><br><span>- component availability</span><br><span>- runtime / seam stability from the mid-Phase-4 hardening pass</span><br><br><span>The weaker areas are:</span><br><span>- final UX ordering and spacing rhythm</span><br><span>- proof / evidence visual cohesion</span><br><span>- palette discipline and color restraint</span><br><span>- production image quality</span><br><span>- final republish gate</span><br><br><span>## Brand anchor</span><br><span>Pacific Engineering should feel like a serious Bay Area engineering and construction partner defined by competence, clarity, and decades worth of wide-ranging field expertise.</span><br><br><span>The site should prioritize:</span><br><span>- trust</span><br><span>- proof</span><br><span>- hierarchy</span><br><span>- composure</span><br><span>- practical project credibility</span><br><br><span>It should avoid:</span><br><span>- flashy over-animation</span><br><span>- startup-like UI language</span><br><span>- vague or over-compressed copy</span><br><span>- decorative motion that competes with evidence</span><br><br><span>## Verified strategic content anchor</span><br><span>The service and positioning language remains aligned with the one-pager:</span><br><span>- Consulting Engineers &amp; Contractors</span><br><span>- Construction Service</span><br><span>- Engineering Consulting</span><br><span>- Inspections &amp; Testing</span><br><span>- Stormwater Planning</span><br><span>- Bay Area jurisdictional familiarity</span><br><span>- compliance-minded delivery</span><br><br><span>Project evidence source set remains:</span><br><span>- Port of San Francisco</span><br><span>- Caltrans</span><br><span>- SFUSD</span><br><span>- SFPUC</span><br><span>- SFO Terminal 3 / Boarding Area E</span><br><span>- Chief Medical Examiner Building</span><br><br><span>## Current execution state</span><br><span>We are still in Phase 4.</span><br><br><span>### Phase status</span><br><span>- Phase 1: mostly complete, residual PostCSS warning remains</span><br><span>- Phase 2: largely complete</span><br><span>- Phase 3: partially complete, seams preserved</span><br><span>- Phase 4: in progress, polish + reliability closeout remaining</span><br><span>- Phase 5: not complete, production imagery pass still needed</span><br><span>- Phase 6: not complete, final republish gate still needed</span><br><br><span>## Mid-Phase-4 hardening result</span><br><span>The mid-Phase-4 hardening run is clean for runtime/seam stability:</span><br><span>- full Playwright matrix passed</span><br><span>- functional flows passed</span><br><span>- focused 5-round loops passed</span><br><span>- public API and internal portal seams unchanged in behavior</span><br><br><span>Artifacts baseline:</span><br><span>- `artifacts/e2e/20260412-0421`</span><br><br><span>QA docs:</span><br><span>- `docs/internal/e2e-step4-runlog.md`</span><br><span>- `docs/internal/e2e-step4-punchlist.md`</span><br><br><span>## Open non-blockers from the hardening pass</span><br><span>- `PostCSS from` warning remains visible and tracked</span><br><span>- legacy QA expectation references `Civil Design`, but current gallery taxonomy uses `Civil + Stormwater`</span><br><br><span>## Image and asset reality</span><br><span>Current production-image quality is not finished:</span><br><span>- project gallery visuals still rely on generated data-URI SVGs</span><br><span>- team/blog/previous-work still include stock or external URLs</span><br><br><span>Required asset direction:</span><br><span>- serve publishable assets from `client/public`</span><br><span>- keep originals/reference inputs in `attached_assets`</span><br><span>- preserve current public API shapes while changing image value sources to static public URLs</span><br><br><span>## Contract and seam rules (locked)</span><br><span>Do not break:</span><br><span>- `GET /api/blog-posts`</span><br><span>- `GET /api/blog-posts/slug/:slug`</span><br><span>- `GET /api/gallery-projects`</span><br><span>- `GET /api/gallery-projects/slug/:slug`</span><br><span>- `POST /api/form-submissions`</span><br><span>- `POST /api/chatbot`</span><br><br><span>Internal seam behavior must remain unchanged:</span><br><span>- no auth coupling changes</span><br><span>- no method/route renames</span><br><span>- no required payload/type changes</span><br><span>- any server/shared changes must be additive and backward-compatible only</span><br><br><span>Treat as contract-locked:</span><br><span>- `server/routes.ts`</span><br><span>- `server/marketingStubService.ts`</span><br><span>- `shared/marketing-content.ts`</span><br><span>- `shared/schema.ts`</span><br><span>- `client/src/portals/lib/apiClient.ts`</span><br><br><span>## Immediate next work (Phase 4 completion)</span><br><span>1. close the two remaining S3 items</span><br><span>2. run final desktop-first polish sweep on:</span><br><span>   - `/`</span><br><span>   - `/about`</span><br><span>   - `/project-gallery`</span><br><span>   - `/contact`</span><br><span>   - `/blog`</span><br><span>3. tighten:</span><br><span>   - typography hierarchy</span><br><span>   - nav/dropdown readability</span><br><span>   - section rhythm</span><br><span>   - proof/evidence/gallery cohesion</span><br><span>   - spacing and color discipline</span><br><span>4. rerun Phase-4 acceptance matrix and focused loops</span><br><span>5. publish a Phase-4 closure note with:</span><br><span>   - what changed</span><br><span>   - what was deferred to Phase 5</span><br><span>   - explicit completion criteria</span><br><br><span>## Phase 5</span><br><span>Replace generated/stock-dependent visuals with production-grade assets while preserving API contracts.</span><br><br><span>## Phase 6</span><br><span>Run final screenshot, behavior, performance, and contract regression gate and produce go/no-go documentation.</span><br><br><span>## Tonight’s priority</span><br><span>Do not broaden scope.</span><br><span>Finish marketing site polish and validation first.</span><br><span>Internal portal launch-scope work and microservice reintegration are deferred until marketing is stable.</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
