</li>
<li data-section-id="x5tmxv" data-start="3442" data-end="3630">
<p data-start="3444" data-end="3630">“Why Pacific Engineering” themes around constructability, Bay Area familiarity, and compliance-minded delivery <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_36i_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_36j_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3632" data-end="3733">So Phase 5 is not blocked by strategy or content. It is blocked by <strong data-start="3699" data-end="3732">publishable image replacement</strong>.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="pxxtml" data-start="3735" data-end="3768">Phase 6 — final republish gate</h2>
<p data-start="3769" data-end="3815"><strong data-start="3769" data-end="3815">Status: not started, but now well prepared</strong></p>
<p data-start="3817" data-end="3887">You already have a stronger baseline than most teams do at this point.</p>
<hr data-start="3889" data-end="3892">
<h1 data-section-id="1ktvpqn" data-start="3894" data-end="3939">What is still needed to get Phase 1 to 100%</h1>
<p data-start="3941" data-end="3967">This is now a narrow task.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="31j869" data-start="3969" data-end="4008">Phase 1 is not missing “restoration”</h2>
<p data-start="4009" data-end="4061">It is missing <strong data-start="4023" data-end="4060">warning elimination at the source</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="jgcaef" data-start="4063" data-end="4129">To get Phase 1 fully closed, you still need all five of these:</h3>
<h2 data-section-id="e91gy2" data-start="4131" data-end="4175">1. Identify the true owner of the warning</h2>
<p data-start="4176" data-end="4276">You already have a doc called <code data-start="4206" data-end="4231">POSTCSS-FROM-WARNING.md</code>, which means discovery has likely been done.</p>
<p data-start="4278" data-end="4311">So the remaining question is not:</p>
<ul data-start="4312" data-end="4346">
<li data-section-id="1k5wblu" data-start="4312" data-end="4346">
<p data-start="4314" data-end="4346">“where does the warning appear?”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4348" data-end="4354">It is:</p>
<ul data-start="4355" data-end="4429">
<li data-section-id="d0wnfg" data-start="4355" data-end="4429">
<p data-start="4357" data-end="4429"><strong data-start="4357" data-end="4429">“what exact code path or dependency is responsible for emitting it?”</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4431" data-end="4470">You need that resolved to one of these:</p>
<ul data-start="4471" data-end="4552">
<li data-section-id="18henzb" data-start="4471" data-end="4493">
<p data-start="4473" data-end="4493">your own config/code</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1h2acuy" data-start="4494" data-end="4526">
<p data-start="4496" data-end="4526">a build tool integration layer</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1a7f0y8" data-start="4527" data-end="4552">
<p data-start="4529" data-end="4552">a dependency/plugin bug</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="1qtpk7b" data-start="4554" data-end="4609">2. Determine whether it is local or dependency-owned</h2>
<p data-start="4610" data-end="4635">That distinction matters.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="j0sfoj" data-start="4637" data-end="4655">If it is local</h3>
<p data-start="4656" data-end="4685">Fix it now and close Phase 1.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="b77zaz" data-start="4687" data-end="4716">If it is dependency-owned</h3>
<p data-start="4717" data-end="4767">Then Phase 1 reaches 100% only after one of these:</p>
<ul data-start="4768" data-end="4986">
<li data-section-id="14vilbm" data-start="4768" data-end="4804">
<p data-start="4770" data-end="4804">version pin or upgrade resolves it</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="19begr1" data-start="4805" data-end="4829">
<p data-start="4807" data-end="4829">patch-package fixes it</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1px0muq" data-start="4830" data-end="4884">
<p data-start="4832" data-end="4884">wrapper config fixes it by passing <code data-start="4867" data-end="4873">from</code> explicitly</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1t4sp8w" data-start="4885" data-end="4986">
<p data-start="4887" data-end="4986">the warning is proven upstream-only and quarantined with an intentional, owned remediation decision</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="shtfvx" data-start="4988" data-end="5035">3. Remove the warning without suppressing it</h2>
<p data-start="5036" data-end="5075">You already locked this rule correctly.</p>
<p data-start="5077" data-end="5093">The fix must be:</p>
<ul data-start="5094" data-end="5185">
<li data-section-id="5w4zqm" data-start="5094" data-end="5108">
<p data-start="5096" data-end="5108">source-level</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="bmekai" data-start="5109" data-end="5129">
<p data-start="5111" data-end="5129">compatibility-safe</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1nayupc" data-start="5130" data-end="5146">
<p data-start="5132" data-end="5146">no suppression</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="tu11zn" data-start="5147" data-end="5185">
<p data-start="5149" data-end="5185">no “just ignore warnings” workaround</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="one0j0" data-start="5187" data-end="5245">4. Re-prove utility output remains stable after the fix</h2>
<p data-start="5246" data-end="5271">Once you fix the warning:</p>
<ul data-start="5272" data-end="5467">
<li data-section-id="ikf6jx" data-start="5272" data-end="5293">
<p data-start="5274" data-end="5293">run <code data-start="5278" data-end="5293">npm run build</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1pu8znr" data-start="5294" data-end="5379">
<p data-start="5296" data-end="5379">run at least a focused visual smoke on <code data-start="5335" data-end="5338">/</code>, <code data-start="5340" data-end="5358">/project-gallery</code>, <code data-start="5360" data-end="5370">/contact</code>, <code data-start="5372" data-end="5379">/blog</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="19y4801" data-start="5380" data-end="5430">
<p data-start="5382" data-end="5430">confirm no class generation changed unexpectedly</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1deiqwp" data-start="5431" data-end="5467">
<p data-start="5433" data-end="5467">confirm no CSS ordering regression</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id="1vdh7mf" data-start="5469" data-end="5498">5. Update the closure note</h2>
<p data-start="5499" data-end="5539">Once the warning is actually eliminated:</p>
<ul data-start="5540" data-end="5651">
<li data-section-id="k00td4" data-start="5540" data-end="5572">
<p data-start="5542" data-end="5572">amend the Phase 4 closure note</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1hxuaf7" data-start="5573" data-end="5601">
<p data-start="5575" data-end="5601">mark Phase 1 as truly 100%</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1fggpoe" data-start="5602" data-end="5651">
<p data-start="5604" data-end="5651">note what changed and where the ownership lived</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="5653" data-end="5656">
<h1 data-section-id="1gzyikj" data-start="5658" data-end="5713">What I would have Codex do next for the PostCSS issue</h1>
<p data-start="5715" data-end="5814">I would not use Codex for broad UX work first.<br data-start="5761" data-end="5764">
I would use it for a tight technical closure pass.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="18mae71" data-start="5816" data-end="5829">Codex task</h2>
<p data-start="5830" data-end="5860">Have Codex do this exact task:</p>
<h3 data-section-id="16s1dnt" data-start="5862" data-end="5875">Objective</h3>
<p data-start="5876" data-end="5988">Eliminate the <code data-start="5890" data-end="5904">PostCSS from</code> warning at the source without suppressing it and without changing runtime behavior.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="77rc8c" data-start="5990" data-end="5999">Scope</h3>
<p data-start="6000" data-end="6013">Inspect only:</p>
<ul data-start="6014" data-end="6257">
<li data-section-id="1tcuvzn" data-start="6014" data-end="6034">
<p data-start="6016" data-end="6034"><code data-start="6016" data-end="6034">postcss.config.*</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1t9f6vg" data-start="6035" data-end="6056">
<p data-start="6037" data-end="6056"><code data-start="6037" data-end="6056">tailwind.config.*</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1cmz4gb" data-start="6057" data-end="6075">
<p data-start="6059" data-end="6075"><code data-start="6059" data-end="6075">vite.config.ts</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1sl5dse" data-start="6076" data-end="6128">
<p data-start="6078" data-end="6128">any CSS build helpers or custom PostCSS processors</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="lp3121" data-start="6129" data-end="6189">
<p data-start="6131" data-end="6189">any place the repo explicitly calls PostCSS <code data-start="6175" data-end="6189">process(...)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1icunen" data-start="6190" data-end="6257">
<p data-start="6192" data-end="6257">lockfile / dependency versions if the warning is dependency-owned</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="f26lga" data-start="6259" data-end="6275">Deliverables</h3>
<ul data-start="6276" data-end="6437">
<li data-section-id="b6uiof" data-start="6276" data-end="6288">
<p data-start="6278" data-end="6288">root cause</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="4fmdsd" data-start="6289" data-end="6326">
<p data-start="6291" data-end="6326">ownership (<code data-start="6302" data-end="6309">local</code> vs <code data-start="6313" data-end="6325">dependency</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1o3t8f" data-start="6327" data-end="6332">
<p data-start="6329" data-end="6332">fix</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1r3ic6j" data-start="6333" data-end="6354">
<p data-start="6335" data-end="6354">why the fix is safe</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="fwplew" data-start="6355" data-end="6389">
<p data-start="6357" data-end="6389"><code data-start="6357" data-end="6372">npm run build</code> output after fix</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="18gdtbm" data-start="6390" data-end="6437">
<p data-start="6392" data-end="6437">confirmation that utility output is unchanged</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="zl2dd9" data-start="6439" data-end="6457">Stop condition</h3>
<p data-start="6458" data-end="6524">Do not move back into broader UX work until the warning is either:</p>
<ul data-start="6525" data-end="6633">
<li data-section-id="bd0bfa" data-start="6525" data-end="6537">
<p data-start="6527" data-end="6537">eliminated</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="b7sp93" data-start="6538" data-end="6633">
<p data-start="6540" data-end="6633">or conclusively proven to be upstream dependency behavior requiring a pinned package strategy</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="6635" data-end="6638">
<h1 data-section-id="yk69hn" data-start="6640" data-end="6669">My practical interpretation</h1>
<p data-start="6671" data-end="6681">Right now:</p>
<ul data-start="6683" data-end="6948">
<li data-section-id="1imnbb9" data-start="6683" data-end="6772">
<p data-start="6685" data-end="6772"><strong data-start="6685" data-end="6696">Phase 4</strong> is probably done enough to move on, <strong data-start="6733" data-end="6772">if <code data-start="6738" data-end="6753">HomeRecovered</code> is actually live</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="hw9omc" data-start="6773" data-end="6840">
<p data-start="6775" data-end="6840"><strong data-start="6775" data-end="6786">Phase 1</strong> is the one phase that still has a technical loose end</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1st7rvh" data-start="6841" data-end="6900">
<p data-start="6843" data-end="6900"><strong data-start="6843" data-end="6854">Phase 5</strong> is now the most important design/content task</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1d4hpcp" data-start="6901" data-end="6948">
<p data-start="6903" data-end="6948"><strong data-start="6903" data-end="6914">Phase 6</strong> is ready once imagery is replaced</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6950" data-end="6986">So the highest-leverage sequence is:</p>
<h2 data-section-id="1jtn53u" data-start="6988" data-end="7006">Immediate order</h2>
<ol data-start="7007" data-end="7170">
<li data-section-id="1qcip6g" data-start="7007" data-end="7068">
<p data-start="7010" data-end="7068">verify the live homepage route (<code data-start="7042" data-end="7057">HomeRecovered</code> vs <code data-start="7061" data-end="7067">Home</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="xhsbe9" data-start="7069" data-end="7104">
<p data-start="7072" data-end="7104">close the PostCSS <code data-start="7090" data-end="7096">from</code> warning</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="6cwdjf" data-start="7105" data-end="7139">
<p data-start="7108" data-end="7139">begin Phase 5 asset replacement</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1088ebn" data-start="7140" data-end="7170">
<p data-start="7143" data-end="7170">then run Phase 6 final gate</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="7172" data-end="7175">
<h1 data-section-id="1ai60qh" data-start="7177" data-end="7212">My recommendation in one sentence</h1>
<p data-start="7214" data-end="7378">You are no longer blocked by architecture or UX strategy — you are blocked by <strong data-start="7292" data-end="7336">one lingering build-warning closure task</strong> and then the <strong data-start="7350" data-end="7377">production imagery pass</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="7380" data-end="7528">If you want, I can turn this into a <strong data-start="7416" data-end="7475">Codex prompt specifically for finishing Phase 1 to 100%</strong>, followed by a separate <strong data-start="7500" data-end="7527">Phase 5 execution brief</strong>.</p>
