2\. Phase 5 execution brief — production imagery and asset quality pass
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

You are working in branch \`chillin\_v2\` of \`last\_breath\`.  
  
Objective:  
Run Phase 5: replace generated, placeholder, stock-dependent, or externally hosted marketing imagery with production-grade, publishable assets while preserving all public API contracts and internal portal seams.  
  
Strategic context:  
\- The marketing site positioning is already correct:  
  - Consulting Engineers &amp; Contractors  
  - Bay Area / Northern California relevance  
  - engineering + construction depth  
  - inspections, stormwater, compliance, and documentation discipline  
  - “Why Pacific Engineering” differentiation grounded in practical judgment and decades worth of wide-ranging field expertise. :contentReference\[oaicite:0\]{index=0} :contentReference\[oaicite:1\]{index=1}  
\- The strongest project-proof source set is already known:  
  - Port of San Francisco  
  - Caltrans  
  - SFUSD  
  - SFPUC  
  - SFO Terminal 3 / Boarding Area E  
  - Chief Medical Examiner Building. :contentReference\[oaicite:2\]{index=2} :contentReference\[oaicite:3\]{index=3}  
\- Phase 4 desktop-first polish is effectively complete.  
\- This pass is about image realism, publishability, consistency, and asset governance.  
  
Locked constraints:  
\- Preserve exact behavior for:  
  - GET /api/blog-posts  
  - GET /api/blog-posts/slug/:slug  
  - GET /api/gallery-projects  
  - GET /api/gallery-projects/slug/:slug  
  - POST /api/form-submissions  
  - POST /api/chatbot  
\- No auth coupling changes.  
\- No required payload/type changes in shared contracts.  
\- Any server/shared change must be additive and backward-compatible only.  
\- Keep:  
  - image: string  
  - images: string\[\]  
  field shapes intact.  
  
Asset policy:  
\- Publishable assets should be served from:  
  - client/public/images/projects  
  - client/public/images/team  
  - client/public/images/blog  
\- Source/reference/original material can remain in:  
  - attached\_assets  
\- Do not actively serve production marketing imagery from attached\_assets.  
\- If generated visual helpers exist, quarantine them as fallback or legacy, but stop active use in the published marketing flow.  
  
Task:  
1\. Inventory all currently non-production imagery on the marketing site:  
   - generated visuals  
   - stock/external URLs  
   - placeholders  
   - weak-quality assets  
2\. Build a replacement map for:  
   - homepage featured proof/work  
   - project gallery  
   - project detail pages  
   - team section  
   - blog cards/posts  
   - any “previous work” or supporting visuals  
3\. Prioritize replacement in this order:  
   - homepage and featured work  
   - project gallery and project detail  
   - about/team  
   - blog  
4\. Store final production-safe assets in \`client/public/images/...\`  
5\. Preserve current contract shapes by changing image value sources only, not the public response schema.  
6\. Add an asset manifest with:  
   - slug/person/post key  
   - public URL  
   - alt text  
   - caption or provenance note  
   - optional source/reference note  
7\. Ensure no broken image regressions across:  
   - /  
   - /about  
   - /project-gallery  
   - project detail  
   - /blog  
   - blog detail  
8\. Keep generated visual code paths present only if needed as inactive fallback. Do not delete unless clearly safe.  
  
Source material emphasis:  
Use the approved project references to make the site feel regionally credible and institutionally trusted:  
\- Port of San Francisco demolition estimate + roof inspection / solar consulting   
\- Caltrans drainage / ADA / signal / stormwater work   
\- SFUSD bond program civil, survey, grading, stormwater, and permit coordination   
\- SFPUC demolition / utility / hazardous materials / SWPPP monitoring work   
\- SFO Terminal 3 / Boarding Area E design-build civil scope   
\- Chief Medical Examiner Building survey and excavation support   
  
Quality standard:  
The final visual system should feel:  
\- serious  
\- Bay Area grounded  
\- technically competent  
\- construction-professional  
\- quietly premium  
\- proof-forward, not decorative  
  
Avoid:  
\- stock-photo obviousness  
\- AI-looking or synthetic project art  
\- glossy SaaS aesthetics  
\- mismatched color temperature and grading across cards/pages  
\- inconsistent crop quality or aspect ratios  
  
Validation:  
After replacements:  
\- run build/check  
\- run a broken-image scan  
\- run public-route visual sanity checks  
\- confirm no public API shape changes  
\- confirm no internal seam drift  
  
Deliverables:  
\- changed file list  
\- asset inventory before/after  
\- asset manifest path  
\- route coverage list  
\- any deferred asset gaps  
\- note on whether generated visuals are still present and whether they are active or quarantined

