<li data-section-id="10bzj1x" data-start="1605" data-end="1716">
<p data-start="1607" data-end="1716">Chief Medical Examiner Building <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_37p_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">example projects completed</p></button></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_37q_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">example projects completed</p></button></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1p05y26" data-start="1717" data-end="2154">
<p data-start="1719" data-end="2154">the service and positioning foundation is still correct, so this phase should improve realism and trust rather than re-open strategy: Construction Service, Engineering Consulting, Inspections &amp; Testing, Stormwater Planning, plus the “Why Pacific Engineering?” differentiation logic around constructability, Bay Area familiarity, and compliance-minded delivery <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_37r_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_37s_" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#554074" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Union</p></button></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2156" data-end="2195">Below is the Codex-ready Phase 5 brief.</p>
<hr data-start="2197" data-end="2200">
<h1 data-section-id="53oa59" data-start="2202" data-end="2277">Codex Execution Brief — Phase 5 Production Imagery and Asset Quality Pass</h1>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="2279" data-end="16037"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy"><div class="cm-scroller"><div class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly"><span>You are working in branch `chillin_v2` of `last_breath`.</span><br><br><span>Objective:</span><br><span>Run Phase 5: replace generated, placeholder, stock-dependent, weak-quality, or externally hosted marketing imagery with production-grade, publishable assets while preserving all public API contracts, shared type shapes, and internal portal seams.</span><br><br><span>This is now the primary active phase.</span><br><span>Phase 1 is considered complete.</span><br><span>Phase 4 desktop-first polish/hardening is considered complete enough to move forward.</span><br><span>Do not reopen structural UX work unless an asset replacement reveals a clear visual break.</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>1. Strategic intent</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>This pass is not a redesign.</span><br><span>It is an asset realism, publishability, consistency, and governance pass.</span><br><br><span>The marketing site positioning is already correct and should remain intact:</span><br><span>- Consulting Engineers &amp; Contractors</span><br><span>- Bay Area / Northern California relevance</span><br><span>- engineering + construction depth</span><br><span>- inspections, stormwater, compliance, and documentation discipline</span><br><span>- “Why Pacific Engineering” differentiation grounded in practical judgment and decades worth of wide-ranging field expertise</span><br><br><span>The strongest approved proof set remains:</span><br><span>- Port of San Francisco</span><br><span>- Caltrans</span><br><span>- SFUSD</span><br><span>- SFPUC</span><br><span>- SFO Terminal 3 / Boarding Area E</span><br><span>- Chief Medical Examiner Building</span><br><br><span>The visual goal is to make the site feel:</span><br><span>- serious</span><br><span>- Bay Area grounded</span><br><span>- technically competent</span><br><span>- construction-professional</span><br><span>- quietly premium</span><br><span>- proof-forward, not decorative</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>2. Locked constraints</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Preserve exact public API behavior for:</span><br><span>- GET /api/blog-posts</span><br><span>- GET /api/blog-posts/slug/:slug</span><br><span>- GET /api/gallery-projects</span><br><span>- GET /api/gallery-projects/slug/:slug</span><br><span>- POST /api/form-submissions</span><br><span>- POST /api/chatbot</span><br><br><span>Internal seam rules:</span><br><span>- no auth coupling changes</span><br><span>- no route/method renames or removals</span><br><span>- no required payload/type changes in shared contracts</span><br><span>- any server/shared change must be additive and backward-compatible only</span><br><br><span>Contract-locked files:</span><br><span>- server/routes.ts</span><br><span>- server/marketingStubService.ts</span><br><span>- shared/marketing-content.ts</span><br><span>- shared/schema.ts</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/lib/apiClient.ts</span><br><br><span>Type-shape lock:</span><br><span>- preserve `image: string`</span><br><span>- preserve `images: string[]`</span><br><span>- change only the value sources, not the shape</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>3. Repo facts to work from</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>- Vite alias `@assets` points to `attached_assets`</span><br><span>- app root is `client`</span><br><span>- build output is `dist/public`</span><br><span>- production-safe public marketing assets should be served from `client/public/...`, not from `attached_assets`</span><br><span>- current marketing routes in scope:</span><br><span>  - /</span><br><span>  - /about</span><br><span>  - /contact</span><br><span>  - /services</span><br><span>  - /services-overview</span><br><span>  - /inspections-testing</span><br><span>  - /special-inspections</span><br><span>  - /structural-engineering</span><br><span>  - /construction</span><br><span>  - /project-gallery</span><br><span>  - /project/:slug</span><br><span>  - /previous-work</span><br><span>  - /blog</span><br><span>  - /blog/:slug</span><br><span>  - /swppp-checker</span><br><span>  - /consultation</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>4. Phase 5 Definition of Done</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Phase 5 is complete when all of the following are true:</span><br><br><span>1. No public marketing route depends on generated placeholder art, obvious stock visuals, weak-quality placeholders, or external image URLs where a production-safe replacement is expected.</span><br><span>2. Production-safe image assets are stored under:</span><br><span>   - client/public/images/projects</span><br><span>   - client/public/images/team</span><br><span>   - client/public/images/blog</span><br><span>3. Source/reference/original inputs remain in attached_assets only as internal source material.</span><br><span>4. Existing API response shapes are unchanged.</span><br><span>5. Broken-image scan is clean on all public marketing routes.</span><br><span>6. Visual consistency is materially improved:</span><br><span>   - crop quality</span><br><span>   - aspect-ratio consistency</span><br><span>   - color temperature consistency</span><br><span>   - better subject matter fit</span><br><span>   - proof-forward image selection</span><br><span>7. Generated visual helpers remain only if quarantined as fallback or legacy and are no longer active in the published marketing flow.</span><br><span>8. Route-by-route validation is documented.</span><br><span>9. Any missing or deferred assets are explicitly listed.</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>5. Asset policy</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Use this policy without exception:</span><br><br><span>A. Public production asset locations</span><br><span>- client/public/images/projects</span><br><span>- client/public/images/team</span><br><span>- client/public/images/blog</span><br><br><span>B. Reference/original holding area</span><br><span>- attached_assets</span><br><br><span>C. Do not actively serve public site imagery from:</span><br><span>- attached_assets</span><br><span>- external stock URLs</span><br><span>- data URI SVG generators</span><br><span>- throwaway placeholders</span><br><br><span>D. If generated visual helpers or old fallbacks still exist:</span><br><span>- keep them only as quarantined legacy/fallback paths</span><br><span>- do not delete unless clearly safe</span><br><span>- remove them from active marketing output</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>6. Current likely targets to inspect first</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Inspect and inventory image usage across these files first:</span><br><br><span>Marketing data / content sources:</span><br><span>- shared/marketing-content.ts</span><br><span>- any gallery/project seed data files</span><br><span>- any blog data source</span><br><span>- any team/profile data source</span><br><span>- any generated visual helper such as project-visuals.ts or equivalent</span><br><br><span>Marketing UI consumers:</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/HomeRecovered.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Home.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/About.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/ProjectGalleryRecovered.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/ProjectGallery.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/ProjectDetail.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/PreviousWork.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Blog.tsx</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/pages/BlogPost.tsx</span><br><span>- any shared CTA / hero / featured work component consuming image props</span><br><br><span>Explicit current signals already known:</span><br><span>- Blog hero still uses an external Unsplash background image</span><br><span>- About still contains an external Unsplash image</span><br><span>- PreviousWork uses project.image</span><br><span>- ProjectDetail uses project.images[]</span><br><br><span>Treat these as evidence that this phase should focus on data and asset replacement, not component redesign.</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>7. Execution order</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Run the pass in this order:</span><br><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><span>Pass A — inventory</span><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><br><span>1. Build a complete image inventory for all public marketing surfaces.</span><br><span>2. For each usage, classify the asset as:</span><br><span>   - generated data-URI / synthetic</span><br><span>   - external stock / hosted offsite</span><br><span>   - internal placeholder</span><br><span>   - acceptable production candidate</span><br><span>   - approved production asset</span><br><span>3. Record:</span><br><span>   - route</span><br><span>   - component/file</span><br><span>   - field source</span><br><span>   - current URL/value source</span><br><span>   - asset type classification</span><br><span>   - replacement priority</span><br><span>   - notes</span><br><br><span>Output:</span><br><span>- docs/internal/phase5-image-inventory.md</span><br><span>- optionally a machine-readable JSON inventory under artifacts or docs/internal</span><br><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><span>Pass B — replacement map</span><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><br><span>Build a replacement map in this order of priority:</span><br><br><span>Tier 1</span><br><span>- homepage hero-adjacent featured proof/work</span><br><span>- homepage project evidence / gallery teaser</span><br><span>- featured work cards</span><br><span>- project gallery cards and map popups</span><br><span>- project detail hero/carousel images</span><br><br><span>Tier 2</span><br><span>- about/team</span><br><span>- previous work</span><br><span>- supporting section imagery</span><br><br><span>Tier 3</span><br><span>- blog featured images</span><br><span>- blog list images</span><br><span>- blog post hero images</span><br><br><span>For each asset family, define:</span><br><span>- destination path under client/public/images/...</span><br><span>- final filename pattern</span><br><span>- slug/person/post mapping</span><br><span>- alt text</span><br><span>- optional caption / provenance</span><br><span>- fallback rule if no approved asset exists yet</span><br><br><span>Output:</span><br><span>- docs/internal/phase5-asset-map.md</span><br><span>- public asset manifest file in repo (see section 9)</span><br><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><span>Pass C — implement production asset serving</span><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><br><span>1. Create folders if missing:</span><br><span>- client/public/images/projects</span><br><span>- client/public/images/team</span><br><span>- client/public/images/blog</span><br><br><span>2. Place production-safe assets there.</span><br><span>3. Update data sources so all active public image values resolve to public URLs under `/images/...`</span><br><span>4. Preserve:</span><br><span>- `image: string`</span><br><span>- `images: string[]`</span><br><br><span>5. Do not break older consumers.</span><br><span>6. Prefer editing central content/data sources over changing many component render paths.</span><br><span>7. If a component currently accepts a direct URL string, keep that behavior and change the values only.</span><br><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><span>Pass D — quarantine generated/legacy image paths</span><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><br><span>1. Find any generated visual helper still in active use.</span><br><span>2. Remove active usage from marketing output.</span><br><span>3. Keep the code only if needed as a documented fallback/legacy path.</span><br><span>4. Add a short note in code or docs stating:</span><br><span>   - legacy/generated</span><br><span>   - not active in production marketing flow</span><br><span>   - retained temporarily for fallback only</span><br><br><span>Do not delete unless clearly safe.</span><br><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><span>Pass E — route-by-route verification</span><br><span>--------------------------------</span><br><br><span>Verify visual coverage on:</span><br><span>- /</span><br><span>- /about</span><br><span>- /project-gallery</span><br><span>- /project/:slug</span><br><span>- /previous-work</span><br><span>- /blog</span><br><span>- /blog/:slug</span><br><br><span>Check for:</span><br><span>- broken images</span><br><span>- off-brand stock feel</span><br><span>- inconsistent crop ratios</span><br><span>- inconsistent color temperature</span><br><span>- weak placeholder feel</span><br><span>- layout shifts introduced by image dimension changes</span><br><span>- missing alt text</span><br><span>- cards with empty visual slots</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>8. Approved source emphasis for imagery choices</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Use the approved project references as the primary visual story backbone.</span><br><br><span>Priority projects:</span><br><span>- Port of San Francisco demolition estimate + roof inspection / solar consulting</span><br><span>- Caltrans drainage / ADA / signal / stormwater work</span><br><span>- SFUSD bond program civil, survey, grading, stormwater, and permit coordination</span><br><span>- SFPUC demolition / utility / hazardous materials / SWPPP monitoring work</span><br><span>- SFO Terminal 3 / Boarding Area E design-build civil scope</span><br><span>- Chief Medical Examiner Building survey and excavation support</span><br><br><span>Image selection rules:</span><br><span>- prefer real project photography or publishable approved visuals</span><br><span>- prefer infrastructure, utility, public works, inspection, construction, structural, surveying, and Bay Area context</span><br><span>- avoid generic office team tropes</span><br><span>- avoid glossy commercial stock that looks unrelated to PECI work</span><br><span>- avoid images that imply capabilities not represented in the source materials</span><br><span>- avoid over-dramatic cityscape hero overload unless used sparingly and intentionally</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>9. Asset manifest requirement</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Add an asset manifest that acts as the source of truth for production imagery.</span><br><br><span>Suggested location:</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/marketing/data/assetManifest.ts</span><br><span>or</span><br><span>- shared/marketing-asset-manifest.ts</span><br><span>(choose the smallest safe scope; prefer marketing-local unless shared usage is required)</span><br><br><span>Suggested shape:</span><br><span>- key / slug / id</span><br><span>- routeFamily or contentType</span><br><span>- publicUrl</span><br><span>- alt</span><br><span>- caption</span><br><span>- sourceNote</span><br><span>- status (approved / provisional / deferred)</span><br><br><span>At minimum cover:</span><br><span>- projects</span><br><span>- team profiles</span><br><span>- blog posts</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>10. Quality bar</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>The final visual system should feel:</span><br><span>- serious</span><br><span>- regionally credible</span><br><span>- technically grounded</span><br><span>- construction-professional</span><br><span>- cohesive across pages</span><br><span>- proof-forward</span><br><br><span>Avoid:</span><br><span>- obvious stock-photo energy</span><br><span>- AI-looking or synthetic art</span><br><span>- generic SaaS gloss</span><br><span>- mismatched color grading</span><br><span>- muddy or low-resolution images</span><br><span>- random aspect-ratio shifts</span><br><span>- decorative visuals that overpower project evidence</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>11. Validation</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>After implementation, run:</span><br><br><span>1. Build/check</span><br><span>- npm run check</span><br><span>- npm run build</span><br><span>- npm run check:repo-hygiene</span><br><br><span>2. Visual/route sanity</span><br><span>- public-route sweep on:</span><br><span>  - /</span><br><span>  - /about</span><br><span>  - /project-gallery</span><br><span>  - /project/:slug</span><br><span>  - /previous-work</span><br><span>  - /blog</span><br><span>  - /blog/:slug</span><br><br><span>3. Broken-image scan</span><br><span>- confirm no 404s or empty image slots</span><br><span>- confirm every intended image renders</span><br><br><span>4. Contract validation</span><br><span>- verify no public API shape changes</span><br><span>- verify no internal seam drift</span><br><br><span>5. Regression note</span><br><span>- note whether payload values changed only by URL source</span><br><span>- confirm no response schema changes</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>12. Deliverables</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Return all of the following:</span><br><br><span>1. Changed file list</span><br><span>2. Asset inventory before/after</span><br><span>3. Asset manifest path</span><br><span>4. Route coverage list</span><br><span>5. Any deferred asset gaps</span><br><span>6. Note on whether generated visuals are:</span><br><span>   - removed from active use</span><br><span>   - quarantined as fallback</span><br><span>   - still present anywhere active</span><br><span>7. Build/check results</span><br><span>8. Broken-image scan result</span><br><span>9. Short quality summary:</span><br><span>   - what is materially more publishable now</span><br><span>   - what still needs later curation</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>13. Non-goals</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Do not:</span><br><span>- reopen Phase 4 polish work except where a replaced image causes a clear visual defect</span><br><span>- redesign components</span><br><span>- change public API shape</span><br><span>- start internal portal launch-scope work</span><br><span>- reintegrate microservices</span><br><span>- suppress warnings as a shortcut</span><br><span>- broaden into unrelated content rewrites</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>14. Success criterion</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>When this pass is done, the marketing site should no longer look like it relies on generated placeholders or external stock imagery.</span><br><span>It should feel materially closer to a publishable, trusted Bay Area engineering/construction brand with a coherent, production-safe asset system.</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="16039" data-end="16042">
<h2 data-section-id="1p8jznt" data-start="16044" data-end="16108">My implementation notes for you before you hand this to Codex</h2>
<p data-start="16110" data-end="16408">The most important repo fact to preserve is this: <code data-start="16160" data-end="16169">@assets</code> still points to <code data-start="16186" data-end="16203">attached_assets</code>, while the app builds from <code data-start="16231" data-end="16239">client</code> to <code data-start="16243" data-end="16256">dist/public</code>, so public-facing assets should move under <code data-start="16300" data-end="16326">client/public/images/...</code>, not remain served from <code data-start="16351" data-end="16368">attached_assets</code> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_37v_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/vite.config.ts" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/vite.config.ts" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">vite.config</p></a></span></p>
<p data-start="16410" data-end="16663">Also, <code data-start="16416" data-end="16434">MarketingApp.tsx</code> still routes all the public surfaces that need image verification in this phase, including <code data-start="16526" data-end="16529">/</code>, <code data-start="16531" data-end="16539">/about</code>, <code data-start="16541" data-end="16559">/project-gallery</code>, <code data-start="16561" data-end="16577">/project/:slug</code>, <code data-start="16579" data-end="16595">/previous-work</code>, <code data-start="16597" data-end="16604">/blog</code>, and <code data-start="16610" data-end="16623">/blog/:slug</code> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_380_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/MarketingApp.tsx" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/MarketingApp.tsx" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">MarketingApp</p></a></span></p>
<p data-start="16665" data-end="16766">And there are already visible non-production image usages in the current code that justify this pass:</p>
<ul data-start="16767" data-end="17329">
<li data-section-id="lui113" data-start="16767" data-end="16917">
<p data-start="16769" data-end="16917"><code data-start="16769" data-end="16779">Blog.tsx</code> hero still uses an external Unsplash background, and blog cards depend on <code data-start="16854" data-end="16870">featured_image</code> values <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_381_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Blog.tsx" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/Blog.tsx" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Blog</p></a></span></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="369fvc" data-start="16918" data-end="17038">
<p data-start="16920" data-end="17038"><code data-start="16920" data-end="16931">About.tsx</code> still contains an external Unsplash image for the expertise visual <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_382_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/About.tsx" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/About.tsx" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">About</p></a></span></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="bt6idf" data-start="17039" data-end="17329">
<p data-start="17041" data-end="17329"><code data-start="17041" data-end="17059">PreviousWork.tsx</code> and marketing <code data-start="17074" data-end="17093">ProjectDetail.tsx</code> render <code data-start="17101" data-end="17116">project.image</code> / <code data-start="17119" data-end="17137">project.images[]</code>, which means Codex should prioritize data-source replacement and asset manifests rather than component rewrites <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_383_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/PreviousWork.tsx" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/PreviousWork.tsx" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">PreviousWork</p></a></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_384_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/ProjectDetail.tsx" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/5a5789ff689084607bb574308db53fa3ffc02f32/client/src/portals/marketing/pages/ProjectDetail.tsx" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">ProjectDetail</p></a></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="17331" data-end="17421">Once Codex finishes this pass, I can build the Gemini review prompt specifically to catch:</p>
<ul data-start="17422" data-end="17587" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">
<li data-section-id="1qsr7pt" data-start="17422" data-end="17455">
<p data-start="17424" data-end="17455">anything that still looks stock</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1sydse7" data-start="17456" data-end="17493">
<p data-start="17458" data-end="17493">anything that still feels synthetic</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="fdlmdp" data-start="17494" data-end="17524">
<p data-start="17496" data-end="17524">inconsistent crops / grading</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="qtos15" data-start="17525" data-end="17587" data-is-last-node="">
<p data-start="17527" data-end="17587" data-is-last-node="">any imagery that weakens the Pacific Engineering brand tone.</p>
</li>
