ked the current <code data-start="22" data-end="34">chillin_v2</code> branch state through the files your Phase 5 pass would have touched.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="1msgxz8" data-start="105" data-end="119">Bottom line</h2>
<p data-start="121" data-end="189">Codex’s summary is <strong data-start="140" data-end="188">materially accurate on the asset-system side</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="191" data-end="282">This is <strong data-start="199" data-end="235">more than just headline removals</strong>. The branch now has a real Phase 5 foundation:</p>
<ul data-start="283" data-end="539">
<li data-section-id="nm5y57" data-start="283" data-end="318">
<p data-start="285" data-end="318">a shared marketing asset manifest</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1oye76x" data-start="319" data-end="370">
<p data-start="321" data-end="370">marketing content resolving through that manifest</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1i1ldfa" data-start="371" data-end="463">
<p data-start="373" data-end="463">external / generated / <code data-start="396" data-end="405">@assets</code> active image paths removed from the public marketing flow</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1q5lo5c" data-start="464" data-end="539">
<p data-start="466" data-end="539">route-by-route inventory and validation docs showing the migration status</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="541" data-end="623">But it is <strong data-start="551" data-end="577">not the end of Phase 5</strong> in the “fully publishable imagery” sense yet.</p>
<p data-start="625" data-end="649">It is best described as:</p>
<p data-start="651" data-end="787"><strong data-start="651" data-end="708">Phase 5 infrastructure and source migration: complete</strong><br data-start="708" data-end="711">
<strong data-start="711" data-end="787">Phase 5 final curation and approved asset replacement: still in progress</strong></p>
<hr data-start="789" data-end="792">
<h1 data-section-id="uasy8e" data-start="794" data-end="834"><span role="text">What I verified in branch <code data-start="822" data-end="834">chillin_v2</code></span></h1>
<h2 data-section-id="12xwgtf" data-start="836" data-end="877">1. The new shared asset system is real</h2>
<p data-start="878" data-end="935">There is now a shared <code data-start="900" data-end="929">marketing-asset-manifest.ts</code> with:</p>
<ul data-start="936" data-end="1175">
<li data-section-id="ssk752" data-start="936" data-end="993">
<p data-start="938" data-end="993">typed asset status: <code data-start="958" data-end="993">approved | provisional | deferred</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="n0enj3" data-start="994" data-end="1017">
<p data-start="996" data-end="1017">project asset entries</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="2w5d2v" data-start="1018" data-end="1038">
<p data-start="1020" data-end="1038">team asset entries</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="reo3jg" data-start="1039" data-end="1059">
<p data-start="1041" data-end="1059">blog asset entries</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1k2urlw" data-start="1060" data-end="1081">
<p data-start="1062" data-end="1081">route image entries</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1dcwadb" data-start="1082" data-end="1175">
<p data-start="1084" data-end="1175">resolver functions for project, blog, and team assets <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_38j_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/shared/marketing-asset-manifest.ts" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/shared/marketing-asset-manifest.ts" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">marketing-asset-manifest</p></a></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1177" data-end="1329">That is a meaningful architectural improvement. It centralizes image governance instead of leaving image references scattered through pages and content.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="epo1xz" data-start="1331" data-end="1401">2. Marketing content now resolves image values through the manifest</h2>
<p data-start="1402" data-end="1444"><code data-start="1402" data-end="1431">shared/marketing-content.ts</code> now imports:</p>
<ul data-start="1445" data-end="1499">
<li data-section-id="7kaquk" data-start="1445" data-end="1470">
<p data-start="1447" data-end="1470"><code data-start="1447" data-end="1470">getMarketingBlogAsset</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15cxpy7" data-start="1471" data-end="1499">
<p data-start="1473" data-end="1499"><code data-start="1473" data-end="1499">getMarketingProjectAsset</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1501" data-end="1774">and maps gallery/blog image values through the manifest-backed source instead of old direct/generated paths. The project entries still preserve <code data-start="1645" data-end="1660">image: string</code> and <code data-start="1665" data-end="1683">images: string[]</code>, which is exactly what we wanted for contract safety <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_38k_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/shared/marketing-content.ts" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/shared/marketing-content.ts" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">marketing-content</p></a></span></p>
<p data-start="1776" data-end="1869">That means the public API shape can stay stable while the image source changes underneath it.</p>
