<h1 data-section-id="19o9bpp" data-start="6360" data-end="6388">2. Gemini execution prompt</h1>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="6390" data-end="9220"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy"><div class="cm-scroller"><div class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly"><span>Unzip the attached codebase and read through it completely, including tracked and untracked files, to understand the current implementation state of branch `chillin_v2`.</span><br><br><span>You are not starting from scratch.</span><br><span>You are entering a repo where:</span><br><span>- Phase 1 is complete</span><br><span>- Phase 4 desktop-first polish/hardening is effectively complete</span><br><span>- Phase 5 infrastructure/source migration is already complete</span><br><span>- the current active task is Phase 5B: turning provisional/local asset coverage into a more publishable, visually coherent, approved-quality image system</span><br><br><span>Your task is to review the current codebase and return a highly practical Phase 5B assessment and plan.</span><br><br><span>## Instructions</span><br><br><span>### 1. Verify current implementation from code</span><br><span>Do not trust assumptions.</span><br><span>Confirm from the repo:</span><br><span>- where the marketing asset manifest lives</span><br><span>- how project/blog/team/route images are currently resolved</span><br><span>- which routes/pages consume those assets</span><br><span>- whether generated/legacy fallbacks are still present and whether they are active or quarantined</span><br><span>- whether any external/stock-like paths remain active</span><br><br><span>### 2. Assess current imagery quality and visual fit</span><br><span>Review current asset usage on the marketing site with attention to:</span><br><span>- route-by-route consistency</span><br><span>- project relevance</span><br><span>- crop quality</span><br><span>- aspect-ratio consistency</span><br><span>- color temperature and grading consistency</span><br><span>- whether visuals support trust and proof</span><br><span>- whether any imagery still feels temporary, stock-like, weak, repetitive, synthetic, or off-brand</span><br><br><span>### 3. Prioritize recommendations</span><br><span>Give recommendations in priority order:</span><br><span>1. homepage / featured proof / gallery teaser</span><br><span>2. project gallery and project detail</span><br><span>3. about/team</span><br><span>4. blog</span><br><br><span>### 4. Stay within constraints</span><br><span>Do not propose:</span><br><span>- breaking API changes</span><br><span>- auth/seam coupling changes</span><br><span>- redesigning the site from scratch</span><br><span>- major component rewrites unless image quality issues create a clear need</span><br><span>- changing public response shapes for `image`, `images`, or `featured_image`</span><br><br><span>### 5. Use Nano-Banana thoughtfully</span><br><span>If appropriate, recommend how Nano-Banana could help with:</span><br><span>- crop harmonization</span><br><span>- lighting/contrast cleanup</span><br><span>- composition consistency</span><br><span>- color temperature normalization</span><br><span>- creating route-consistent derived variants from approved original assets</span><br><br><span>But do not recommend synthetic visuals that undermine trust for a construction/engineering brand.</span><br><br><span>## Deliverables</span><br><br><span>Return:</span><br><span>1. repo-state verification summary</span><br><span>2. current Phase 5 completion estimate</span><br><span>3. route-by-route imagery review</span><br><span>4. list of remaining provisional assets that matter most</span><br><span>5. list of assets that are already good enough</span><br><span>6. concrete next-pass instructions for Codex</span><br><span>7. Nano-Banana assistance opportunities</span><br><span>8. recommendation:</span><br><span>   - proceed to Phase 6</span><br><span>   - or complete one more Phase 5B pass first</span><br><br><span>Make your review specific, operational, and grounded in what the codebase actually contains.</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
