dden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="21cfa074-7b7d-4b76-a5b1-5eeac7b542b3" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/0.98 relative rounded-[22px] px-4 py-2.5 leading-6 max-w-(--user-chat-width,70%)"><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Would we benefit by allowing codex to use figma here or should we wait til phase 6 to integrate figma's canvas with codex?

and yes - now write the Gemini review prompt for this exact Phase 5B state.
</div></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex justify-end"><div aria-label="Your message actions" class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto touch:opacity-100 duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" role="group" tabindex="-1" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy message" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Edit message" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#6d87e1" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div><span class="sr-only"><br></span></section><section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="5c3a3557-4286-4908-a64b-8c5e7ee2fb95" data-testid="conversation-turn-75" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h4 class="sr-only select-none">ChatGPT said:</h4><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="b895a58d-ed33-4489-b750-902e0728ecbc" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-4-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="217" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">I’m checking the Figma-related skills against your current Phase 5B state first so the recommendation is grounded in the right workflow, then I’ll give you the Gemini review prompt tailored to this exact branch state.</p></div></div></div><div class="my-2 flex w-full flex-col gap-2"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1"><button type="button" aria-disabled="false" class="text-token-text-tertiary inline-flex w-full items-start text-start text-base cursor-pointer hover:underline"><span class="line-clamp-1 truncate">Used figma-internal-scout skill.</span></button><button type="button" aria-disabled="false" class="text-token-text-tertiary inline-flex w-full items-start text-start text-base cursor-pointer hover:underline"><span class="line-clamp-1 truncate">Used figma-to-code-contract skill.</span></button></div></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><button type="button" class="text-token-text-tertiary flex items-center gap-0.5 dark:text-(--interactive-label-tertiary-default) hover:text-token-text-primary dark:hover:text-token-text-primary">Thought for 37s<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon-xs"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#b140e7" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="7cb22a96-b279-4e2c-a360-f2e9c9c6ebc3" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-4-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="55">Yes — but <strong data-start="10" data-end="54">only in a narrow, surgical way right now</strong>.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="1p30mkq" data-start="57" data-end="97">My recommendation on Figma with Codex</h2>
<h3 data-section-id="rv7y25" data-start="99" data-end="135"><span role="text">Use Figma <strong data-start="113" data-end="120">now</strong>, but only for:</span></h3>
<ul data-start="136" data-end="402">
<li data-section-id="c6mvai" data-start="136" data-end="211">
<p data-start="138" data-end="211">final visual verification of <strong data-start="167" data-end="211">team/blog remaining provisional surfaces</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1p1fv3x" data-start="212" data-end="304">
<p data-start="214" data-end="304">checking <strong data-start="223" data-end="276">crop hierarchy, spacing balance, and image weight</strong> on the key marketing routes</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1b90kct" data-start="305" data-end="402">
<p data-start="307" data-end="402">resolving any last “does this feel right?” disagreements on homepage, gallery, or about layouts</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1nkvay0" data-start="404" data-end="437"><span role="text">Do <strong data-start="411" data-end="418">not</strong> use Figma now for:</span></h3>
<ul data-start="438" data-end="645">
<li data-section-id="1afoequ" data-start="438" data-end="475">
<p data-start="440" data-end="475">broad canvas-to-code reconstruction</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="197gfex" data-start="476" data-end="519">
<p data-start="478" data-end="519">reinterpreting the whole marketing system</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="gzqwos" data-start="520" data-end="574">
<p data-start="522" data-end="574">reopening layout architecture that is already stable</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1qt42lq" data-start="575" data-end="645">
<p data-start="577" data-end="645">large component rewrites just because the Figma canvas looks cleaner</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1xxfhz4" data-start="647" data-end="654">Why</h3>
<p data-start="655" data-end="669">At this point:</p>
<ul data-start="670" data-end="1103">
<li data-section-id="1e35dy6" data-start="670" data-end="689">
<p data-start="672" data-end="689">Phase 1 is closed</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="irmheu" data-start="690" data-end="735">
<p data-start="692" data-end="735">Phase 4 is effectively closed desktop-first</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="ufki5c" data-start="736" data-end="1103">
<p data-start="738" data-end="1103">Phase 5B has already promoted the six highest-trust project asset families to <code data-start="816" data-end="826">approved</code> and left only team/blog as clearly deferred/provisional, which means the branch is now in a <strong data-start="919" data-end="940">review-and-finish</strong> state rather than a <strong data-start="961" data-end="983">design-from-canvas</strong> state <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_3ce_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/shared/marketing-asset-manifest.ts" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/shared/marketing-asset-manifest.ts" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">marketing-asset-manifest</p></a></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_3cf_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/docs/internal/phase5b-curation-note.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/docs/internal/phase5b-curation-note.md" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">phase5b-curation-note</p></a></span> <span class="relative inline-flex items-center select-none" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="radix-_r_3cg_" data-state="closed"><a href="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/docs/internal/phase5-image-inventory.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath/blob/chillin_v2/docs/internal/phase5-image-inventory.md" class="ms-1 relative flex h-[25px] select-none items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded-xl px-2 text-[10px] leading-[13px] corner-superellipse/1.1 text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">phase5-image-inventory</p></a></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1105" data-end="1141">So the best use of Figma <strong data-start="1130" data-end="1137">now</strong> is:</p>
<ul data-start="1142" data-end="1380">
<li data-section-id="11ipt04" data-start="1142" data-end="1268">
<p data-start="1144" data-end="1268"><strong data-start="1144" data-end="1179">Figma Internal Scout style work</strong>: inspect specific nodes/screens and verify design intent against the live implementation</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1v12907" data-start="1269" data-end="1380">
<p data-start="1271" data-end="1380"><strong data-start="1271" data-end="1308">Figma to Code Contract style work</strong>: only if one or two surfaces still need precise implementation guidance</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1ddhygr" data-start="1382" data-end="1400">Practical rule</h3>
<p data-start="1401" data-end="1456">Use Figma now <strong data-start="1415" data-end="1455">only when tied to a specific surface</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1457" data-end="1544">
<li data-section-id="1vwbati" data-start="1457" data-end="1486">
<p data-start="1459" data-end="1486">homepage hero / proof block</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1eppjrr" data-start="1487" data-end="1499">
<p data-start="1489" data-end="1499">about/team</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="zpmfkl" data-start="1500" data-end="1517">
<p data-start="1502" data-end="1517">project gallery</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="l95f5" data-start="1518" data-end="1544">
<p data-start="1520" data-end="1544">blog cards / blog detail</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1546" data-end="1619">Do <strong data-start="1549" data-end="1556">not</strong> do a general “integrate Figma with Codex” pass before Phase 6.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="qupicr" data-start="1621" data-end="1636">Short answer</h2>
<ul data-start="1637" data-end="1763">
<li data-section-id="13ugh3v" data-start="1637" data-end="1687">
<p data-start="1639" data-end="1687"><strong data-start="1639" data-end="1647">Yes:</strong> allow limited Figma-assisted review now</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="kvbbx2" data-start="1688" data-end="1763">
<p data-start="1690" data-end="1763"><strong data-start="1690" data-end="1697">No:</strong> do not do full Figma-canvas integration as a broad workstream yet</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1765" data-end="1933">The right moment for full canvas/code alignment is <strong data-start="1816" data-end="1825">after</strong> Phase 5 is truly closed or <strong data-start="1853" data-end="1863">during</strong> Phase 6 only if final gate screenshots expose a real design mismatch.</p>
<hr data-start="1935" data-end="1938">
<h1 data-section-id="g41uza" data-start="1940" data-end="1999">Gemini review prompt for the exact current Phase 5B state</h1>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="2001" data-end="8314"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-a066ed1a.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy"><div class="cm-scroller"><div class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly"><span>You are reviewing a zipped local copy of branch `chillin_v2` from:</span><br><span>https://github.com/dylanlmeraki/last_breath.git</span><br><br><span>Your task is to review the repo in its **current Phase 5B state** and determine whether the marketing site is ready to proceed into Phase 6, or whether it needs one more narrow asset-curation pass first.</span><br><br><span>This is a **review + recommendation pass**, not a redesign pass.</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>Current branch state you should assume and verify</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Phase 1:</span><br><span>- complete</span><br><br><span>Phase 4:</span><br><span>- effectively complete in a desktop-first sense</span><br><span>- runtime, layout hardening, seam protection, and route stability are already in a good state</span><br><br><span>Phase 5:</span><br><span>- asset-system migration is complete</span><br><span>- active external stock URLs are removed from the public marketing flow</span><br><span>- active `@assets` marketing image serving is removed from the public marketing flow</span><br><span>- active generated-image usage is removed from the public marketing flow</span><br><span>- centralized marketing asset governance is in place</span><br><br><span>Phase 5B:</span><br><span>- six Tier 1 proof-project asset families were promoted from `provisional` to `approved`</span><br><span>- these six are the trust backbone:</span><br><span>  - Port of San Francisco</span><br><span>  - Caltrans</span><br><span>  - SFUSD</span><br><span>  - SFPUC</span><br><span>  - SFO Terminal 3 / Boarding Area E</span><br><span>  - Chief Medical Examiner Building</span><br><span>- team assets remain provisional</span><br><span>- blog assets remain provisional</span><br><span>- route coverage sweep is clean</span><br><span>- broken-image / source-policy / seam checks are clean</span><br><br><span>This means the current question is **not** whether the asset system works.</span><br><span>The current question is whether the current imagery set is **good enough to move into Phase 6**, or whether one more small curation pass is warranted.</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>Repo/implementation constraints</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Do not recommend:</span><br><span>- breaking API changes</span><br><span>- auth coupling changes</span><br><span>- route/method renames</span><br><span>- required payload/type changes</span><br><span>- changes to the public image field shapes:</span><br><span>  - `image: string`</span><br><span>  - `images: string[]`</span><br><span>  - `featured_image` string behavior</span><br><br><span>Treat these as contract-sensitive:</span><br><span>- server/routes.ts</span><br><span>- server/marketingStubService.ts</span><br><span>- shared/marketing-content.ts</span><br><span>- shared/schema.ts</span><br><span>- client/src/portals/lib/apiClient.ts</span><br><br><span>The asset system should continue to be driven by the existing shared marketing manifest and local `/images/...` paths.</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>Brand guardrails</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Pacific Engineering should feel:</span><br><span>- serious</span><br><span>- Bay Area grounded</span><br><span>- technically competent</span><br><span>- construction-professional</span><br><span>- quietly premium</span><br><span>- proof-forward</span><br><span>- shaped by decades worth of wide-ranging field expertise</span><br><br><span>Avoid:</span><br><span>- glossy SaaS aesthetics</span><br><span>- generic stock-photo energy</span><br><span>- AI-looking or synthetic project imagery</span><br><span>- decorative visuals that overpower trust</span><br><span>- overly trend-driven visual choices</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>What I want you to do</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>1. Unzip the attached codebase and read it thoroughly, including tracked and untracked files.</span><br><span>2. Verify from the repo:</span><br><span>   - current marketing asset manifest state</span><br><span>   - which assets are `approved` vs `provisional`</span><br><span>   - which routes/pages consume those assets</span><br><span>   - whether any external/generated paths remain active</span><br><span>3. Review the current imagery on the marketing routes and tell me whether the current branch is:</span><br><span>   - ready for Phase 6</span><br><span>   - or one small curated pass away from Phase 6</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>Routes to review carefully</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Primary review routes:</span><br><span>- /</span><br><span>- /about</span><br><span>- /project-gallery</span><br><span>- /project/:slug</span><br><span>- /previous-work</span><br><span>- /blog</span><br><span>- /blog/:slug</span><br><br><span>Secondary sanity routes:</span><br><span>- /contact</span><br><span>- /services</span><br><span>- /services-overview</span><br><span>- /inspections-testing</span><br><span>- /special-inspections</span><br><span>- /structural-engineering</span><br><span>- /construction</span><br><span>- /swppp-checker</span><br><span>- /consultation</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>What to evaluate on each route</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Evaluate:</span><br><span>- whether the imagery feels project-specific and believable</span><br><span>- whether the strongest proof projects are being visually prioritized</span><br><span>- whether any visuals still feel stock-like, generic, repetitive, weak, synthetic, or placeholder-driven</span><br><span>- crop quality</span><br><span>- aspect-ratio consistency</span><br><span>- color temperature / grading consistency</span><br><span>- whether visuals strengthen trust or merely fill space</span><br><span>- whether team/blog provisional imagery is acceptable for relaunch or still too weak</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>Output format</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Return the following sections:</span><br><br><span>1. **Repo-state verification**</span><br><span>   - confirm current manifest/asset architecture</span><br><span>   - confirm current approved/provisional split</span><br><span>   - confirm whether any active external/generated paths remain</span><br><br><span>2. **Current Phase 5 completion estimate**</span><br><span>   - give your estimate in %</span><br><span>   - justify it briefly</span><br><br><span>3. **Route-by-route imagery assessment**</span><br><span>   For:</span><br><span>   - /</span><br><span>   - /about</span><br><span>   - /project-gallery</span><br><span>   - /project/:slug</span><br><span>   - /previous-work</span><br><span>   - /blog</span><br><span>   - /blog/:slug</span><br><br><span>   For each, say:</span><br><span>   - strong</span><br><span>   - acceptable but provisional</span><br><span>   - weak and should be improved before Phase 6</span><br><br><span>4. **Most important remaining visual debts**</span><br><span>   - rank the top remaining weak spots by trust impact</span><br><br><span>5. **What is already good enough**</span><br><span>   - list the areas that should not be reopened unnecessarily</span><br><br><span>6. **Recommendation**</span><br><span>   Choose one:</span><br><span>   - proceed directly to Phase 6</span><br><span>   - or do one small Phase 5C cleanup pass first</span><br><br><span>7. **If a Phase 5C pass is needed**</span><br><span>   - specify exactly what that pass should include</span><br><span>   - keep it narrow and practical</span><br><br><span>8. **Optional Nano-Banana opportunities**</span><br><span>   Only include if genuinely useful.</span><br><span>   Limit suggestions to:</span><br><span>   - crop harmonization</span><br><span>   - background cleanup</span><br><span>   - headshot consistency</span><br><span>   - archival upscaling</span><br><span>   - tonal harmonization</span><br><br><span>Do not recommend synthetic project generation.</span><br><br><span>==================================================</span><br><span>Decision criterion</span><br><span>==================================================</span><br><br><span>Be strict but practical.</span><br><br><span>Do not ask whether the site is perfect.</span><br><span>Ask whether the current branch is credible, cohesive, and trustworthy enough to move into the final republish gate without creating obvious brand drag.</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="8316" data-end="8401">If you want, after Gemini responds, send me that output and I’ll turn it into either:</p>
<ul data-start="8402" data-end="8480" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">
<li data-section-id="oy14zo" data-start="8402" data-end="8439">
<p data-start="8404" data-end="8439">a <strong data-start="8406" data-end="8435">tiny Phase 5C Codex brief</strong>, or</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="s2eq9o" data-start="8440" data-end="8480" data-is-last-node="">
<p data-start="8442" data-end="8480" data-is-last-node="">a <strong data-start="8444" data-end="8479">Phase 6 go/no-go execution plan</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul></div></div></div></div><div class="relative h-[60px] select-none"><div class="absolute h-[60px]" style="opacity: 1;"><button class="not-prose group/footnote border-token-border-default bg-token-main-surface-primary hover:bg-token-main-surface-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 mt-3 mb-2 flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl border py-2 ps-3 pe-2.5"><div class="flex flex-row-reverse gap-1"><div class="border-token-main-surface-primary bg-token-main-surface-primary flex items-center overflow-hidden group-hover/footnote:border-token-main-surface-secondary relative" style="opacity: 1;"><div class="icon-sm"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-external-a5a181b2.svg#1a6f23" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></div></div></div><div class="text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-0.5 text-xs font-semibold">Sources</div></button></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div aria-label="Response actions" class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" role="group" tabindex="-1" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy response" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-ce